{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw","id":1200645,"title":"Oh look, a bandwagon, watch me jump on it, or: where I read Dragon-Blooded:WFHW","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-28T17:16:12-07:00","id":1200645,"title":"Oh look, a bandwagon, watch me jump on it, or: where I read Dragon-Blooded:WFHW","content":"This seems to be in vogue.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm not sure that the forum needs three different topics of various people working their way through the book, but hey, I may as well open a topic on the forums instead of spamming the Skype group of my Exalted players with my impressions as I go along. <div align=\"center\">***</div> <br /> <br /> I'm not a big fan of chapter fiction in general (albeit I still find them preferable to 2E's comics which often made me want to disappear from the face of the earth with secondhand embarrassment). However, I found the one at the very beginning of the core really entertaining and worthwhile, so I'm going to make an exception to my usual policy and not skip them outright.<br /> <br /> <br /> Three survivors and a plethora of dead bodies, huh? <i>Some people </i>were rolled into a battle group, I see.<br /> <br /> Interesting to see how readily the remnants of the Realm's force accept the two newcomers. Albeit I suppose they're not in a position to be picky - and it's obvious that Mathar is not here as an official representative of Lookshy. Still, I can't help but think about how common this sort of thing is, random strangers showing up uninvited to Wyld Hunts, offering their assistance.<br /> <br /> Oh, it's because he was already tracking them. Nevermind, then.<br /> <br /> The rest of the chapter fiction is, for lack of a better term, uneventful, I guess? Our heroes swear the oath of kinship, then proceed to fight the two exhausted Anathema and win. Interesting that apparently Kinships can be made and and dismissed trivially.<br /> <br /> Dammit, now I can't help but wonder <i>how they work</i>. Can you be in multiple Kinships at once? I seem to recall fairly stringent requirements from an earlier Ask the Devs post, so probably not. Is it common for Dragon-Blooded who have fought side by side for decades to maintain this bond even after they part ways? What mores surround the practice? If a member has to go on an extended assignment somewhere far away, does the Kinship get temporarily disbanded and reassembled when she gets back (because doing so frees her to get the benefits of a Kinship with her local peers, whose status is probably more relevant to her at the moment)? Or is it seen as a more significant commitment? Do the Dragon-Blooded often cling to such bonds out of sentimentality, rejecting to disband or expand a Kinship after key members have fallen? When this happens, how does the wider Dynastic (or Lookshyan, or...) society view it? Inquiring minds wish to know.<br /> <br /> <br /> Introduction! We open with the Romance of the Three Kingdoms quote that has explicitly served as the inspiration behind the idea of a Sworn Kinship, fittingly enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Based on the chapter summaries, it seems that next week we'll get Life in the Scarlet Dynasty and Beyond the Realm. I await these with great interest.<br /> <br /> <br /> Suggested resources! Let's see what we have here...<br /> <br /> <br /> Huh, they put the Mahabharata in here. Not the kind of book that would immediately jump to my mind when thinking about Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> Interestingly enough, this is actually one of those books that were a formative read of my childhood, and it wasn't actually that long ago that I've re-read it. It was a strange experience, because a lot of the tales contained within are <i>super </i>misogynistic, which has not really... registered with me as a child, or at least not in the same way as Greek mythology did. It was easy to understand that Zeus chaining Hera to the sky by the wrists and tying anvils to her ankles was <i>kind of a fucked up thing to do</i>, but the fact that there are a bunch of women in these stories with no agency whatsoever, who literally only exist so that the protagonist can earn their hand in marriage, then almost immediately move on to a new adventure and get a new, functionally identical wife didn't really seem too strange or unusual to me at the age of 10.<br /> <br /> Oh, it also features a monkey who manages to get his testicles crushed by a log that was split halfway. That is literally the extent of what I can recall from this book: &quot;more misogyny than I remembered from my childhood, and a monkey gets its testicles crushed&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Codex Alera sounds really cool from the description we're being given. Yet this is literally the first time I hear about it. I wonder what's up with that. Is it a case of a good concept marred by subpar execution? Or am I just really out of the loop regarding recently published fantasy novels?<br /> <br /> <br /> And, of course, ATLA gets a mention, along with Legend of Korra. I can't help but feel that Legend of Korra is a bit unfairly maligned here - season 3 is actually my favorite of the entire franchise, and in general, people tend to forget how many mediocre-to-bad episodes the original series had.<br /> <br /> ...No, seriously, LoK is <i>fine.</i> It holds up even in comparison to ATLA. (Except for the second season. The second season was utter garbage. ATLA never sunk as far as LoK did at its worst, but I think it also never reached the same heights as it did at its best.)<br /> <br /> (...I always wanted to write a blog post about the way Legend of Korra teaches some really good, really important GMing principles, but my plans of doing so were invariably thwarted by the fact that I don't actually <i>have </i>a blog.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And I think this is a fine place to pause, for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T17:35:11-07:00","id":1200651,"title":"","content":"...Okay, the fact that I literally couldn't remember anything worthwhile about the Mahabharata was bugging me, so I actually took the time to... walk into the next room and grab the book off the shelf.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, I was wrong - the parable of the monkey that got its testicles crushed due to its own stupidity was in the Panchatantra, not in the Mahabharata. In my defense, apparently the book I have is a multiple-volume collection of Sanskrit texts, and the Panchatantra is in the same volume as the excerpts from the Mahabharata. So that should clear up any confusion if somebody looks into the thread and goes &quot;wait, what, I've just read that book and can't remember <i>anything </i>like that&quot;.<br /> <br /> (The point about misogyny may or may not stand - that is not the kind of thing I can immediately verify by flipping through the book and noting that &quot;oh wait, this chapter title I remembered actually belongs in a completely different text&quot;.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-28-2018, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T18:59:20-07:00","id":1200666,"title":"","content":"Re Codex Alera: I think people tend to talk more about his other series, the Dresden Files. That said, I'm not the best person to talk about either of said series.<br /> <br /> As for Legend of Korra, I've been meaning to go watch the third season, but I really don't want to watch the second one. Do you know of any good recaps for what happened in the second season so I'm not lost when I go try to watch the third?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T19:04:10-07:00","id":1200670,"title":"","content":"Carole Sartyamurti has written a very good retelling of the Mahabharata in English blank verse. It recounts the plot of the original epic very accurately while offering more voice and narrative focus to the women and lower-caste characters.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books/about/Mahabharata_A_Modern_Retelling.html?id=ZjVMBAAAQBAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;source=kp_read_button#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.com/books/about...page&amp;q&amp;f=false</a><br /> <br /> Chitra Divakaruni also wrote a novel called &quot;Palace of Illusions&quot;, which retells the Mahabharata from the perspective of Draupadi, wife to the Pandava brothers and incarnation of the Goddess Sri.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.chitradivakaruni.com/books/#/books/palace-of-illusions/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.chitradivakaruni.com/book...-of-illusions/</a><br /> <br /> In response to BrilliantRain:<br /> <br /> The second season of LoK is fairly weak in execution, but you should definitively watch episodes 7-8. Those episodes are pretty self-contained and tell the story of how the first Avatar came into existence: there's beautiful visuals that perfectly capture the Exalted drama of humans trying to survive in a beautiful world overrun with fickle spirits and gods.<br /> <br /> Also, I personally enjoyed Codex Alera immensely: particularly since it was born out of a dare to write a novel that fused the myths of the Lost Roman Legion with Pokemon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","user":"AldoSalt","date":". 03-28-2018, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12641-aldosalt","name":"AldoSalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12641_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T04:17:49-07:00","id":1200757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1200666#post1200666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As for Legend of Korra, I've been meaning to go watch the third season, but I really don't want to watch the second one. Do you know of any good recaps for what happened in the second season so I'm not lost when I go try to watch the third?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you're probably better off not touching a recap. I found the explanation behind the origin of the Avatar Cycle about as necessary as midichlorians, and any summary of events would eventually have to include the fact that in the finale, Korra turns into a glowing giant and has a kaiju battle with Avatar Satan on the shores of Republic City. Also, Avatar Satan has a death ray for some reason. <i>Yet somehow this still manages to be boring</i>.<br /> <br /> Pretty much all you need to know is that there is a planet-wide spiritual convergence, and over the course of events, the separation between the world of humans and spirits ends. Both of those things become plot points in season 3. (Also, if the cheesy teenage romance stuff is a draw for you, I think Korra breaks up with Mako over the course of the season, which may or may not end up being undone by the end of it - I genuinely can't remember.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AldoSalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1200670#post1200670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Carole Sartyamurti has written a very good retelling of the Mahabharata in English blank verse. It recounts the plot of the original epic very accurately while offering more voice and narrative focus to the women and lower-caste characters.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books/about/Mahabharata_A_Modern_Retelling.html?id=ZjVMBAAAQBAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover&amp;source=kp_read_button#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.com/books/about...page&amp;q&amp;f=false</a><br /> <br /> Chitra Divakaruni also wrote a novel called &quot;Palace of Illusions&quot;, which retells the Mahabharata from the perspective of Draupadi, wife to the Pandava brothers and incarnation of the Goddess Sri.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.chitradivakaruni.com/books/#/books/palace-of-illusions/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.chitradivakaruni.com/book...-of-illusions/</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the recommendations!<br /> <br /> Also, can I say that I find it awesome that I can post about an incredibly specific and obscure problem on - in the wider context of the internet - an incredibly specific and obscure board, and in less than two hours, have somebody pop up with &quot;yeah, this incredibly specific and obscure problem you've been having, somebody already solved it, here, have a link&quot;? It's fantastic. <i>You're</i> fantastic, Internet Stranger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> With that out of the way, let's proceed with the next part of our WIR: wherein I analyze the contents of a single page in unreasonable detail!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the next chapter fiction, we get into the head of the Empress herself.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026I have to admit, I have no idea what that stone is supposed to be. The hearthstone of the Imperial Manse, perhaps? My none-too-perfect encyclopedic knowledge of Exalted lore fails me.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the callback to Aspect Book: Air. This is really how callbacks <i>should</i> be done: unobtrusive enough that someone unfamiliar with earlier editions doesn\u2019t lose out on anything, yet still capable of giving veterans a nice and fuzzy \u201eI understood that reference\u201d feeling. It also has the added benefit of firmly centering the scene in the game\u2019s timeline in a way that simply writing down the date doesn\u2019t really do (no, seriously, don\u2019t tell me I\u2019m supposed to know the canonical \u201epresent year\u201d of Exalted off the top of my head).<br /> <br /> <br /> I really like how the description of the murals being made from the five magical materials drives across the decadent opulence of the surroundings. <i>The Empress has murals depicting centuries of her deeds, wrought from jade, moonsilver and orichalcum</i>. Just imagining the scale of that, thinking about how many artifacts could\u2019ve been forged from what\u2019s basically <i>decoration</i> in her palace, really hammers the point home.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Yeah, this is not the corebook\u2019s opening fiction. I\u2019m not entirely sure what is being communicated here (I sincerely hope that posting quotes is okay):<br /> <br /> <i>\u201eHere, alone and naked before her deeds, a single sob escapes her lips. (\u2026) Her Essence is stone and flame, and the fire is ever upon her within her depths. Yet embers can grow cold, she fears, and even mountains can fall to the inexorable sea.</i><br /> <i>It is a moment, though. The seas recede, salt and water vanishing into air.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Why is the Empress crying? Or rather \u2013 why is she crying <i>now</i>? I feel like this passage is meant to humanize her, but it\u2026 doesn\u2019t do a very good job. Is this meant to be a regular occurence? If yes, <i>why</i>? She has ruled the Scarlet Dynasty for centuries \u2013 you would think that she\u2019d have gotten numbed to the day-to-day reality of that. Or is this meant to be a singular moment of weakness, the like of which only happens once in a few decades? But if it\u2019s that, what prompted it? I can buy that she is largely inured to the pressures of\u2026 being who she is, yet every once in a while, things pile up, it becomes too much to bear, and the facade breaks for a brief, private moment \u2013 but why now? A few paragraphs ago, she was calmly thinking about making her current lover a magistrate. There is no real transition between her \u201efocused on getting shit done\u201d state of mind and what we see later. The fleeting moment of humanity feels unearned.<br /> <br /> The imagery also feels confused. First we have this: \u201e<i>Her Essence is stone and flame, and the fire is ever upon her within her depths\u201d</i>, and I\u2019m like, \u201eoh, the writer has managed to work three of the five elements into a brief sentence describing her (with \u2019depths\u2019 being an obvious allusion to water), that\u2019s kinda clever\u201d.<br /> <br /> But then we continue with \u201e<i>Yet embers can grow cold, she fears, and even mountains can fall to the inexorable sea\u201d</i> \u2013 so apparently the sea is now something external (let\u2019s go with \u201ethe slowly grinding pressure that comes with leading the greatest empire on Creation\u201d), and in a single sentence, water suddenly turns into a threat instead of an inalienable portion of the Empress\u2019 very being. I guess it still works as long as the reader is willing to go back and re-interpret the previous sentence \u2013 depths can allude to earth as well, but two out of five elements is considerably less clever than three.<br /> <br /> So far so good, but the next sentence requires an internal re-framing <i>again</i>, with \u201e<i>The seas recede, salt and water vanishing into air</i>\u201d, which is just a flowery way to say that she regains her composure. It <i>kinda</i> works with the earlier \u201ethe sea is a metaphor for external pressure\u201d interpretation, but at the same time, the obvious literal imagery is staring you in the face. Taken in isolation, this is not a bad thing! Art is created in the spaces between the layers of the literal and the metaphorical. The sentence is fine on its own \u2013 but at the same time, if the reader is required to re-evaluate what you\u2019re trying to do with the concept and imagery of water <i>three times in four sentences</i>, maybe you\u2019re overdoing it a bit.<br /> <br /> (Again, this stands in stark contrast with the opening fiction in the core, where it is very clear what every stylistic flourish is meant to evoke or underline.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the touch that attendants are meant to avert their eyes when she\u2019s grasping the crown \u2013 it is described as heavy and she has to socket the stone into it, so my mind immediately jumps to \u201ethis rule was probably made because fiddling with the socketing mechanism while holding the big-ass metal thing with one hand must look somewhat undignified\u201d. The unsaid implications of this throwaway half-sentence manage to humanize her far more effectively than the flowery paragraph we just went over in detail.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaand the rest of the fiction is pretty much what you\u2019d expect \u2013 it turns out that she was preparing for an audience with the signature circle, who show up with a gift Anathema in tow and are rewarded accordingly. Cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well this bit ran slightly longer than I originally planned, so we\u2019ll take it up from here next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-29-2018, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:36:18-07:00","id":1200962,"title":"","content":"Next up is a brief history of the Dragon-Blooded.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don\u2019t actually have anything insightful to say about this that others haven\u2019t already. Yes, it\u2019s nice to see the Dragon-Blooded <i>do things</i> on their own \u2013 Celestials having to <i>request</i> their help in the First Age, with some of them saying \u201efuck no, I have better things to do\u201d and starting their own kingdoms with blackjack and hookers; the Shogunate\u2019s taming of unconquerable territories and the wide-scale destruction that resulted from their conflicts (they blew up Chiaroscuro! The bastards!).<br /> <br /> I <i>adore</i> the Outcaste groups mentioned here. We get a clan of poisoner-assassins in the East, a rogue Imperial legion in the South, a sect of heretics in the West, and a cult of fae-touched Dragon-Blooded in the North. We\u2019re probably going to hear more about them later.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a census of Terrestrials in this section. I find it interesting that apparently there are nearly as many Outcastes in the Realm as there are outside of it in the entirety of Creation (4000 versus 5000). Also, all cadet houses taken together apparently can\u2019t produce as many Dragon-Blooded as an average Dynastic House by itself (750 versus 1000). These are not the numbers I\u2019d have expected. (Also, <i>holy shit the average Dynastic House produces nearly as many Dragon-Blooded scions as an entire Direction outside the Realm</i>. Just how big are these families?)<br /> <br /> <br /> Huh, they explicitly went out of the way to hard cap the age of Dragon-Blooded Exaltation at 20. This kind of rules out the story possibilities of the failed scion, written off by his entire family, suddenly igniting his Essence in the midst of a midlife crisis \u2013 unless shenanigans are involved. (But then again, this is a very shenanigan-friendly edition.)<br /> <br /> Interesting that there\u2019s an entire paragraph about how much of Dynastic adolescence revolves around waiting for the magical moment of Exaltation, but no mention of the stupid and hazardous \u201eHIS CLASSMATES HATE HIM! TRIGGER YOUR EXALTATION WITH THIS ONE WEIRD TRICK\u201d methods that desperate scions experiment with (to no provable effect). I always liked that bit of 1E fluff.<br /> <br /> So apparently the Immaculate Philosophy is not really invented wholecloth, just\u2026 pilfered from the works of First Age philosophers and metaphysicians, and subtly altered. Honestly, it doesn\u2019t make much difference to me either way, but I\u2019ve heard some people say that this makes it more respectable in their eyes, so\u2026 huzzah? Also, I have no idea why has this been put under the chapter about the Dragon-Blooded Exaltation itself.<br /> <br /> An entire page details the subtleties of the moment of Exaltation. I found no groundbreaking insight within, but I like this sentence: \u201e<i>Deaths from the fallout of Terrestrial Exaltation are uncommon \u2014 most people have the sense to leave the area as soon as a child begins to glow with power \u2014 but property damage and injuries are almost guaranteed.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> A lot of words are spent on clarifying how the Elemental Aspect works \u2013 how it is inherited (the children of two people with the same Aspect are likely to be of the same Aspect as well), how it changes a developing person in body and mind, and what the limitations of its influence are (TLDR: it won\u2019t override your entire personality overnight). There\u2019s also a description of every individual Aspect, and their strengths and weaknesses. (This reminds me of an old dev quote, which basically said that the in-universe motivation behind the Immaculate Dragons\u2019 portrayal was largely to steer impressionable Dragon-Blooded away from the negative extremes of behavior their Aspect naturally pulls them towards. Re-reading the core, some of this fits, others\u2026 not so much. On the other hand, I noticed for the first time that the symbols of the Immaculate Dragons on page 72 have little depressions in the direction that corresponds to the Pole of their respective element, which is a nice visual touch!)<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a quote in the section about Essence Fever that I really like:<br /> \u201e<i>A young Terrestrial Exalt not only has to contend with the unfurling power within her, but also the mundane changes she\u2019s undergoing. The Essence of the Dragons is volatile, capable of passionate love and tempestuous rage. A newly Exalted Dragon-Blooded is encouraged to spar and roughhouse to vent these passions. Her Aspect shapes not just her body, but her mind and emotions. She is a tempest, a bonfire, a tsunami, </i>a force of nature <i>given flesh and walking among mortals. Essence seethes and thrashes within her, driving her to be as aloof, passionate, or nurturing as her Aspect dictates.</i>\u201d<br /> It feels like the book is explicitly calling out that this is meant to facilitate cheesy teenage drama in secondary school games. I approve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next time, we\u2019ll continue with Dragon-Blooded societies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-29-2018, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T17:39:28-07:00","id":1201080,"title":"","content":"So, the book has the same kind of \u201eprestige spreads\u201d about the Realm, Lookshy, Prasad, the Forest Witches and Outcastes that the core had about individual Exalt types, which is a pretty clever way to lay out player options.<br /> <br /> The option to be a Dynast is kind of a given, and honestly, I don\u2019t need much convincing to want to play a decadent asshole noble with a superiority complex that would rival Tony Stark\u2019s \u2013 this is pretty much my default mode of play in every game anyway.<br /> <br /> The part about Lookshy fails to convince me that they\u2019re very interesting. They seem like generic soldier dudes without any of the things that make the Realm compelling, and not much of their own in return. \u201eYou get cool toys\u201d is not much of a draw for me in Exalted, where pretty much every character starts out with all the cool toys they\u2019ll ever need.<br /> <br /> Prasad is, of course, fantastic. The thing that makes me feel <i>really</i> interested in it as a setting, however, is this part from the Realm preview: \u201e<i>[T]ainted souls, Wyld mutants, Anathema, and even inhuman monsters such as demons and Fair Folk may surrender to the shikari and seek the wisdom of the Pure Way. Through hard work, obedience, and purifying rituals, unclean creatures seek a cleaner death, and a place in the cycle of reincarnation.</i>\u201d When Lunars come out, one of my campaign pitches will certainly be \u201eso, how would you guys feel about playing a triumvirate of Alucards in not!India ruled by heretical Dragon-Blooded?\u201d.<br /> (Is this idea straining against canon? Probably \u2013 it would be really stupid of the Wyld Hunt to keep around a bunch of Anathema for the specific purpose of dropping them on other Anathema and hoping that they won\u2019t cut and run at the first opportunity. But sometimes, you just want to let your players be Alucard first, and worry about constructing elaborate justifications later. Which is kind of a betrayal against the principles behind Exalted, but... I find myself unable to give much of a fuck about that. A lot of the discourse that surrounds the game is focused on making sure that every tiny detail is in order, internal consistency is meticulously maintained, and tone is strictly controlled \u2013 but when all is said and done, I find the idea of getting too snobby about what amounts to a bunch of grownups sitting down at a table to play make-believe with glowing anime superheroes <i>incredibly absurd</i>.)<br /> (Which is not to say that <i>some</i> amount of snobbery won\u2019t improve your game \u2013 after all, what is snobbery to one person is maintaining basic standards to another. But sweating about the dubious canonicity of a campaign idea is generally not a very productive use of one\u2019s time, I think.)<br /> <br /> The Forest Witches are next, and at this point, I\u2019m very tempted to use them to introduce one of my groups to Exalted. \u201eYou get to play elemental kung-fu demigods plugged into augmented reality\u2026 in a mythical Bronze Age world\u201d is not only an immediately attention-grabbing premise, but it also comes with a strong inbuilt motivation for PCs to get out and interact with the world (the pool must be fed, after all).<br /> <br /> Last but not least are the Outcastes. Much like the Dynasts, I don\u2019t think much convincing is needed to sell people on them, but for the exact opposite reason \u2013 Dynasts are interesting because their place in the setting is concrete and well-defined, with a plethora of character concepts and story hooks a player can build upon, whereas Outcastes are interesting because they can be anyone, slot into anywhere, and have none of the baggage that being a Solar carries (the need for secrecy, the unshakable feeling that you\u2019re playing a Mary Sue, and the trouble of having to justify why you were Chosen \u2013 which limits character concepts to an annoying degree). It\u2019s also a nice touch that the text explicitly calls out that an Outcaste doesn\u2019t actually need to be a rootless folk hero \u2013 deserters, exiles and disgraced Dynasts are perfectly fine concepts as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And that\u2019s the end of the prestige spreads! Next time, we\u2019ll pick up from here with another unnecessarily detailed sequence of complaining about chapter fiction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T17:43:55-07:00","id":1201081,"title":"","content":"Oh I very much approve of the title!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T17:59:18-07:00","id":1201093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201081#post1201081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I very much approve of the title!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I sincerely hope that's not the <i>only </i>thing people are approving of, because I've got to say, the general lack of response to any of the things I say about the ostensible subject of the thread is... disheartening.<br /> <br /> At this point, even a &quot;clearly, you're a barely literate idiot, here's why the chapter fiction with the Empress was secretly genius...&quot; kind of vehement expression of disagreement would be a welcome change of pace :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T18:03:18-07:00","id":1201097,"title":"","content":"Kind of busy still reading the manuscript of this, Trinity Core, Aeon, and Anna Karererererina... :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T18:57:16-07:00","id":1201114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201080#post1201080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Is this idea straining against canon? Probably</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't seem to be; after all, you've just cited the passage stating that they have a principle of allowing the Anathema to try and redeem themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminumtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it would be really stupid of the Wyld Hunt to keep around a bunch of Anathema for the specific purpose of dropping them on other Anathema and hoping that they won\u2019t cut and run at the first opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it would be; that trust must be <i>earned</i>.<br /> <br /> \u200bPossibly with a bit of reinforcement of certain Artifacts to keep them on the straight and narrow, but at some point one has to judge whether or not contrition is genuine and allow a subject the freedom to demonstrate their own changes. Sure, they might prove to have been highly effective liars, but is one willing to take that risk when the value of the good bet is the redemption of a monster's soul?<br /> <br /> \u200bBesides, it's not as if this is all fiat; there are mechanics to mediate the cultivation and awareness of another person's values and motivations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T21:52:52-07:00","id":1201139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201097#post1201097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of busy still reading the manuscript of this, Trinity Core, Aeon, and Anna Karererererina... :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been trying to catch up on Changeling the Lost (never read the manuscript during the KS).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T22:15:43-07:00","id":1201144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201093#post1201093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I sincerely hope that's not the <i>only </i>thing people are approving of, because I've got to say, the general lack of response to any of the things I say about the ostensible subject of the thread is... disheartening.<br /> <br /> At this point, even a &quot;clearly, you're a barely literate idiot, here's why the chapter fiction with the Empress was secretly genius...&quot; kind of vehement expression of disagreement would be a welcome change of pace :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciated your commentary on the chapter fiction. I think you make some good points and possibly a little rewriting on that section to clean up the metaphor might be a smart idea. <br /> <br /> Though, I didn't like the intro fiction for the Core Book, but you piqued my interest and I'd enjoy reading your analysis of it, in the hopes that, regardless how I end up thinking about it, I understand it better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T22:33:14-07:00","id":1201146,"title":"","content":"As regards Alucard and Hellsing and using that as a model for a Solar powered Wyld Hunt (heh), I think the main issue is that the Hellsing Organization has some unspecified control mechanisms that mean Alucard has to obey Integra that seem to be nigh infallible, while, in Creation I really doubt that most people would think that there are any sort of mind control or whatever that could constrain a Solar long term.<br /> <br /> That said, if you WANT to play that game, just create a Sorcerous Oath Binding or an Artifact or whatever that forces them to obey their DB keepers and you should be fine. As long as the players are down with the concept (and you don't have their bosses tug on the leash too hard or too often) they shouldn't spend much of their time struggling against the bindings and you can just sort of place them in ST fiat level territory that no-one worries about, the same way spy games aren't usually about the players plotting to take over MI-6 and/or England.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T02:18:02-07:00","id":1201188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201114#post1201114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't seem to be; after all, you've just cited the passage stating that they have a principle of allowing the Anathema to try and redeem themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think &quot;hard work and obedience&quot;, in this context, means something more... spiritually edifying than punching people. A supernaturally strong Anathema might be put to till the fields, doing the work of ten men in a single day. A Craft-oriented one might be sent to build a dam for a village threatened by floods. And ones without such obvious uses would be doing the kind of activities you'd see monks being sent to do by the titular abbot in the Record of Linji.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201146#post1201146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As regards Alucard and Hellsing and using that as a model for a Solar powered Wyld Hunt (heh), I think the main issue is that the Hellsing Organization has some unspecified control mechanisms that mean Alucard has to obey Integra that seem to be nigh infallible, while, in Creation I really doubt that most people would think that there are any sort of mind control or whatever that could constrain a Solar long term.<br /> <br /> That said, if you WANT to play that game, just create a Sorcerous Oath Binding or an Artifact or whatever that forces them to obey their DB keepers and you should be fine. As long as the players are down with the concept (and you don't have their bosses tug on the leash too hard or too often) they shouldn't spend much of their time struggling against the bindings and you can just sort of place them in ST fiat level territory that no-one worries about, the same way spy games aren't usually about the players plotting to take over MI-6 and/or England.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think the idea works better with Lunars, aesthetically - the more inhuman nature of their powers underlines how their handlers see them: dangerous monsters, to be employed against other monsters as shock troops or a weapon of last resort. It\u2019s also much easier for the players to do <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8GbnMSGXEyE&amp;feature=youtu.be&amp;t=189\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> To me, the control mechanism mostly just seems like \u201eAlucard has a Defining Tie of Loyalty towards any sufficiently \u2019pure\u2019 human who manages to vanquish him\u201d. It\u2019s not externally imposed. Creating a sorcerous oath or an artifact to do this job, therefore, seems to me like a wrong approach to take. Honestly, I was mostly just thinking that they would be pumped full of all sorts of nasty and long-lasting poisons, and get the antidote as long as they remain obedient \u2013 small infractions provoke a temporary withdrawal, and going on the run poses\u2026 difficulties. The nice thing about this approach is that the core explicitly assumes PC exceptionalism, so nothing breaks setting-wise if we say that their handlers have spent months testing the limits of their tolerance and set the dosage based on that, then they\u2019re in for a nasty surprise when it turns out that the party has collectively picked up some poison resistance Charms during gameplay. It not a reasonable assumption for the Wyld Hunt to make that they would develop such an ability in the sort of timeframe the game takes place in. This is important, because half the fun is letting the PCs decide whether they want to turn rogue and exact a terrible vengeance, or go on with the original premise!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Next up: a tangent about the genius of the core's opening fiction!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-30-2018, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T03:39:42-07:00","id":1201198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201188#post1201188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think &quot;hard work and obedience&quot;, in this context, means something more... spiritually edifying than punching people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the very existence of the Wyld Hunt provides an example of how a culture can view punching the right people as spiritually edifying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The nice thing about this approach is that the core explicitly assumes PC exceptionalism, so nothing breaks setting-wise if we say that their handlers have spent months testing the limits of their tolerance and set the dosage based on that, then they\u2019re in for a nasty surprise when it turns out that the party has collectively picked up some poison resistance Charms during gameplay.</div> </div> </div> </div>This puts me in mind of how one thing that I like about the Solar immunity Charms is that they don't immunise you against something that you haven't been hit with before, so it creates a significance to variety in poisons and diseases despite there not being much mechanical variation between them.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It not a reasonable assumption for the Wyld Hunt to make that they would develop such an ability in the sort of timeframe the game takes place in.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wouldn't entirely agree with that, and could see ways to make your idea work within the general outline of the handlers knowing that their countermeasure can't be absolute, but it doesn't really matter to your own game and the kinds of setpiece that you would want.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T04:33:39-07:00","id":1201207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201198#post1201198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the very existence of the Wyld Hunt provides an example of how a culture can view punching the right people as spiritually edifying.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way I see it, the subject of whether &quot;rehabilitated&quot; Anathema should be employed to fight against other Anathema is probably a hotly contested topic in-universe, with some voices indeed arguing that punching Anathema is <i>always</i> morally correct (and moreover, that exposing them to the temptation to cut and run gives them an opportunity to test their virtue and display that they have truly grown beyond their wicked ways), but the dominant conservative viewpoint being that it was the uncontrolled lust for battle that led the Forsaken to blasphemously steal the power of the Unconquered Sun, and the first steps to rehabilitation require at least a few centuries of quiet contemplation and avoiding violence in general. So, basically, the willingness of the adherents of the Pure Way to allow Anathema to participate in Wyld Hunts is heavily dependent on context, influenced by factors such as the currently dominant philosophical approach among religious leaders, questions of expediency (willingness to go for the nuclear option probably skyrockets after the traditional methods of containing a problem have failed), and of course the character of the Anathema in question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201198#post1201198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI wouldn't entirely agree with that, and could see ways to make your idea work within the general outline of the handlers knowing that their countermeasure can't be absolute</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When it comes to controlling a terrifying demon-god of war, no countermeasure can be absolute - but sometimes meticulously re-evaluating the utmost limits of what they can take every few weeks just ends up with the subject building up tolerance even faster, so I imagine they re-calibrate every half a year or so. Which gives players a fairly generous window to buy up Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T07:59:51-07:00","id":1201262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201144#post1201144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, I didn't like the intro fiction for the Core Book, but you piqued my interest and I'd enjoy reading your analysis of it, in the hopes that, regardless how I end up thinking about it, I understand it better.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ask, and ye shall receive. <i>In excruciating detail.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, the opening fiction \u2013 there are three important functions it has to serve. It has to introduce people new to Exalted to some of the concepts within the game, it has to showcase some of the changes between editions, and it should be an enjoyable enough read to not make the reader reflexively want to skip it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, one of the things I find striking about it is the sheer efficiency of the text. Let\u2019s take a look:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThere in that place the sea was still; its waters were stopped up, its currents were broken. The sluice-streets down in the bottom-most layers did not run wet and then dry three times a day, like in the better districts, but simply sat there pooling, seeping, gathering bugs and gunk and plague. They who lived there were scarcely recorded by the men and women who kept the books in Heaven. \u201cSome number of little people reside below,\u201d they\u2019d say, or write, \u201c\u2014and bugs,\u201d and nod their heads.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Immediately in the second paragraph, we are introduced to the concept of Heaven, and get a strong impression of how it is different from, say, the Upper Planes of D&amp;D \u2013 its bureaucracy, its fallibility, its arrogance. (Note that the text says \u201ethe men and women who kept the books in Heaven\u201d \u2013 not angels, not gods, just men and women, prone to writing off those living in the slums as insignificant.)<br /> <br /> It also sets up the origin of our protagonist, which is further elaborated on in the next paragraph:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201eWhen Suzu, the younger of the two, was four, she went out into the sluice-streets to play; only, instead of dying to the hungry dead, or falling into the hands of some flesh-taker, scavenger, or priest, she found a white pig (that her father said was likely sacred), with an earring that was a bell. She\u2019d led it home, she\u2019d loved to keep it, she\u2019d ridden on it and confided in it and drawn great swirling patterns of black ink upon its flesh. She\u2019d tugged on Sabriye\u2019s sleeve\u2014that was the older girl\u2014and told her all about it, and it was a precious pig to little Suzu, and come the winter when they cut it open they found oracles in silvered letters on its bones.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Again, note the economy of words \u2013 we\u2019re only three paragraphs in, but now we have a very concrete image of the kind of place our protagonist grew up in (the slums of Wu-Jian \u2013 stinking, unsanitary, ravaged by plague, slavers and the hungry dead), introduced to the person she came back to see, given a taste of the strangeness that suffuses Creation (you can sometimes run into sacred pigs that are born with silver inscriptions on their bones, and apparently nobody finds this incredibly noteworthy), and shown by implication the mindset of the people who live in the slums. The text reveals just as much by what it omits than it does by what it says out loud: we\u2019re informed in great detail about how much Suzu loved that damn pig, but it is never mentioned that she was particularly saddened when they ate it. Need and practicality rule over emotional attachment, <i>even for a four-year old</i>. This speaks volumes about the circumstances these people live in, and the writer accomplishes this purely by choosing what <i>not</i> to focus on.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next paragraph introduces the reader to the concept of Solar Exaltation \u2013 what it is (\u201e<i>Sabriye had joined the ranks of legends; had done some great unrecorded deed and won Exaltation: drawn down into her body a portion of the essence of the divine Unconquered Sun</i>\u201d), the way previous incarnations work [I](\u201e<i>t was a legacy and a power that had been Liam Island-Tamer\u2019s before her, and Red Dove\u2019s before him, on back to the beginning of the world</i>\u201d), and the tremendous in-setting impact of it (\u201e<i>[t]here was all manner of consternation among the bookkeepers in Heaven at that change; it provoked great flurries of paperwork, anguished tugging of the beards, and Heavenly commotion</i>\u201d). This is the part aimed at newcomers, for whom this might be the first thing they read about Solars.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next part sets up the central conflict of the story, and boy, do I love it:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>She understood only that she had changed. That her steps had lightened, her eyes gone clearer, and a sun-mark glittered on her brow. If she were to try to explain it\u2014 ...there was no explaining it. Words would fail her. Was it some sun-borne curse? The blessing of some small god of river, grass, or tree? Was she, as the Immaculate Faith would surely tell her, shamed and shameful beyond all measuring: indwelt, possessed, inhabited by some Anathematic demon-god?</i><br /> <i>If she knew the truth of it, deep in her soul, then to her mind it yet remained a mystery: a secret that lived beneath her tongue and in her throat. That stuck there, that weighed her down, that pooled in her like stagnant water.</i><br /> <i>The words would not come out.</i><br /> <i>And so, like anyone who has words they cannot speak, she sought out a kindred spirit to not say them to. She returned to Wu-Jian, hunting for the nameless house on the nameless street that her cousin had used to live in\u2014rehearsing as she searched for Suzu all the words she would not say.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> On a technical level, the opening fiction already manages to distinguish itself from the industry average purely on the basis that it actually <i>has</i> a central conflict, and it is resolved by the end. (This is kind of sad.) But the thing that I really like about it is the nature of this central conflict\u2013 it\u2019s not a foe that threatens the protagonist, or some deadly situation she has to extricate herself from: it\u2019s simply the issue of <i>communicating the experience of the change that befell her</i>. This accomplishes two things at the same time: in the mind of the reader, it anchors the Exaltation as a momentuous, transcendent miracle that defies words (an important message for newcomers, but an even more important one for veterans \u2013 much of the discussion around Exaltation still basically treats it as an autonomous missile in some corners of the fan community), but just as important is the fact that it firmly roots the Chosen as having fundamentally human concerns. Not being able to put a feeling or idea into exact words is <i>relatable</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then all of a sudden, Sabriye\u2019s journey of introspection is abandoned with a silky smooth transition, as we go from the difficulties of putting words on the indescribable to a Dragon-Blooded mocking the cuisine of Wu-Jian:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>In this, she was not alone.</i><br /> <i>Ten floors above her, at that time, and three wards left, Jin chewed. Jin swallowed. \u201cI don\u2019t even know how to describe this,\u201d Jin said. He put down his meat bun. He made an ancient finger sign against evil\u2014most specifically, against Anathematic demon-gods\u2014in its general direction. His partner Toad Rat snorted a laugh. \u201cI want to describe it,\u201d said Jin, \u201cbut\u2014there are no words.\u201d</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s a fantastic gag.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026I\u2019m not going to go over the entire text in this level of detail, or we\u2019ll never get back to What Fire Has Wrought. So, just the highlights\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Let us speak of deeps and gutters; of starlight hidden in the darkness; of city piled on city: Of Wu-Jian.</i>\u201d \u2013 the book says, and in a rare moment of synergy between text and layout, we are greeted by the <i>absolutely gorgeous</i> two-page spread of the city upon turning the page. This is technically not a strength of the opening fiction, but I still found it worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> <br /> The story of the outcast islands is conveyed with appropriately mythic imagery, and I also like the in-setting lack of certainty that is conveyed here. The purpose of this section is, again, to introduce newcomers to the ancient deeds of the Solar Exalted, and I think it does a fine enough job of it.<br /> <br /> Another thing I find worth noting here is the effortless way the writer uses language to convey scale.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201e\u2026in that moment of its defenselessness he replaced his pipe, seized a shaft of sunlight from the sky, made it gold, and plunged it like a pillar, like a needle, like a spear, through the body of the island, through the stone and through the sea beneath the island, and made it anchored to the ocean floor.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Drawing out the resolution of the sentence like that creates the impression of the scale of an island-spanning nail in a much more tangible way than just writing \u201eyo, these things were <i>really big</i>\u201d in however flowery a manner would. Then the same tool is employed again to convey the sprawling nature of the city itself:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201e</i><i>Atop that dusting of pinned-down land amidst the endless waters they built a crisscrossing maze of bridges, an iridescent web and stronghold, rising, falling, slanting, sloping, reminiscent in its many angles of a broken-legged spider crouching, injured, on the sea.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying this is high art, mind \u2013 just that the tools the writer uses are employed much more confidently and with a much greater level of conscious intent to reach a specific goal than they are in the chapter fiction of WFHW.<br /> <br /> <br /> Next, we learn something about the Dragon-Blooded \u2013 again, this is for the benefit of newcomers.<br /> <br /> The transition from the expository flashback into the immediate present is pretty good here.<br /> <br /> This entire fight sequence is fantastic and much more dynamic than the one we\u2019ll talk about shortly. The way it shifts into a discussion is also much better executed, not to mention the contents of the discussion \u2013 the characters start to argue about <i>meat buns</i>. This sort of levity serves as an important shout-out to the realities of the gaming table, which I find valuable in gaming fiction.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will never stop adoring the sentence \u201eToad Rat (\u2026) never wanted anything more from life than to have his name well-regarded in society, and, never to have to hunt down and engage in battle with an invincible demon-goddess of war\u201d. The humanization of these throwaway characters is more effective here than the attempt is in the Empress fiction \u2013 the writer only allows the Empress to show weakness in a very narrow and societally approved way even in the privacy of her own home (a point <i>could</i> be made about that in the text, actually, but <i>isn\u2019t</i>), and because of that, the moment feels contrived, rehearsed, theatrical \u2013 a shorthand meant to evoke the <i>idea</i> of humanity instead of the real thing in the messy and undignified way it truly exists. By contrast, Toad Rat is allowed to be slightly cowardly and motivated by the approval of his peers, and Eastern Star is allowed to be a person who constructs elaborate justifications for antagonistic feelings that stem from jealousy and pride, <i>and they are stronger, more memorable characters for that</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> A powerful point is made a bit later, with the way the text calls back to the expository flashback earlier. I\u2019ll quote it:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201e</i><i>Sabriye had loved this tale best. </i><br /> <i>\u201cWe\u2019d dug down,\u201d Sabriye\u2019s aunt had said. \u201cThey came in and they were wreathed in animas of wood and fire, earth and water, wind\u2014they had armor forged in the ancient days and weapons that could shatter buildings in one go\u2014but we dug down, we hid ourselves; we gnawed and nested at the roots of their great grand house like rats. Hated and despised we were, but we were the unconquerable gold; raised up our bosses, us, to extort from them, our thief-kings to steal their goods from them and made our priests and murderers our saints. And in the end they gave in to us. They didn\u2019t have the steel in them to burn us out, to uproot Wu-Jian, and lose their great grand port in the western sea.\u201d </i><br /> <i>She\u2019d grinned with the missing teeth of her, and glee. </i><br /> <i>Years later, Sabriye would remember that grin; hesitating, uncertain, on a roof not far from Suzu\u2019s one-time door, she would remember it, and match it with a smile of her own: </i><br /> <i>\u201cThe demon-gods could tame the sea,\u201d her aunt had said, \u201cand the Dragon-Blooded cast them down\u2014\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>Jin and his heavy spear crashed down; shattered her reverie, burst the roof that Sabriye crouched on, tore through it as she rolled aside.</i><br /> <br /> <i>[\u2026fight scene goes on for two pages\u2026]</i><br /> <br /> <i>To speak of the positioning of her legs, her hips, her hands, would be inadequate to describe it; in that moment, her Essence surged, a radiance\u2014an anima\u2014of sunlight flared up around her, and the whole of her Solar prowess became more than its individual parts. </i><br /> <i>She moved, and it was as if he were seized up by a giant hand. His stance shattered and his breath blew out; his armor seemed to slam tight around his chest; an absurd admiration welled up inside him as inexorably, impossibly, he was lifted up into the air, bent over double, and then slammed down straight. </i><br /> <i>The demon-gods could tame the sea, Sabriye\u2019s aunt had said, so many years ago; and the Dragon-Blooded cast them down\u2014 </i><br /> <i>But they could none of them not stand one whit against the people of Wu-Jian. </i><br /> <i>And Jin passed out.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The one who vanquishes Jin is Sabriye the gutter rat, the nobody from the slums of Wu-Jian, and <i>not</i> Sabriye the Solar Exalt.<br /> <br /> (Some would no doubt say that this is retarded, because in an alternate universe where Sabriye the gutter rat is not <i>also</i> Sabriye the Solar Exalt, the same confrontation would end up with her skewered on the point of a spear. To this, I can only respond with \u201eyou\u2019re missing the point\u201d.)<br /> <br /> (\u2026To which a reasonably smart person could, of course, respond with \u201eno, I got the point just fine, here is how it could have been conveyed in a manner that isn\u2019t self-defeating\u2026\u201d, followed by a proposal of a version of the scene where Sabriye defeats Jin by drawing on her superior knowledge of the surroundings, demonstrating that it is indeed her status as a native of Wu-Jian that earns her the victory \u2013 and they would not necessarily be wrong. Just arguing against a <i>different</i> point than the one being made.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Then Eastern Star is introduced (but I already said what I wanted to say about her), followed by another conversation-turned-fight-scene. This one is fairly tense and desperate.<br /> <br /> Eventually, a massive pig god appears, calls Sabriye one of the Solar Exalted, and the core conflict of the story is resolved. Honestly, this part could\u2019ve been written a bit more artfully. Still, it ends with another fantastic sentence:<br /> <br /> <i>\u201e</i><i>And it seemed to her, in that golden moment, like she might understand the secret that lived beneath her tongue; what it might be that she could tell her cousin Suzu\u2014if she still lived there, if they ever met\u2014before the great wall burst, and she saw the ocean beyond it, and the dawn; and water came rushing in to the sluice-streets, swirling, pouring, flowing, sweeping, pounding, raising her and all that muck towards Heaven like some great paean to the sun.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s some pretty great imagery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-30-2018, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T08:35:26-07:00","id":1201281,"title":"","content":"I could absolutely see something like the Doom of Damocles from the Dresden Files series happening, some Immaculate Monk is convinced that he can be the one to save an Anathema, or even just that Anathema could be saved at all, but has to put his own life on the line as 'collateral' for the Anathema that he wants to allow into the Order; if the PCs screw up, both he and the Anathema's lives are forfeited. It would give the players a humanized face for an otherwise antagonistic organization, as well as a nice central quest-giver for newer players or just people that like that kind of structured setup.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty cool idea, one that I might have to steal for my own now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:48:32-07:00","id":1201305,"title":"","content":"In the clip you linked, Alucard specifically says that he\u2019s encountered a dangerous and powerful opponent, so he\u2019s removing his power limiters until the opponent is dead. That sounds like something more than just an intimacy.<br /> <br /> But yeah, poison might work sure. A long lasting and complex supernatural poison of some kind, yeah, I could see it.<br /> <br /> Edit: I totally missed there was a second page to this thread. Yeah, I like your ideas for controlling Anathema.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 03-30-2018, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T12:36:38-07:00","id":1201362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201207#post1201207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The way I see it</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOf course, there's not a right or wrong answer: it's all about just talking through alternative approaches. I think I've elaborated on my perspective to the highest degree necessary. <br /> <br /> \u200bAnd I mean that as a sincere final word, rather than something passive-aggressive.<br /> <br /> All discussions should be like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI will be interested to see what you say about the rest of the book.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:27:33-07:00","id":1201383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw#post1200645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Codex Alera sounds really cool from the description we're being given. Yet this is literally the first time I hear about it. I wonder what's up with that. Is it a case of a good concept marred by subpar execution? Or am I just really out of the loop regarding recently published fantasy novels?<br /> <br /> <br /> And, of course, ATLA gets a mention, along with Legend of Korra. I can't help but feel that Legend of Korra is a bit unfairly maligned here - season 3 is actually my favorite of the entire franchise, and in general, people tend to forget how many mediocre-to-bad episodes the original series had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you suggest that about Codex Alera, as the series was inspired by a dare to demonstrate the opposite point: that execution transcends concept. Jim Butcher was challenged to make &quot;Lost Roman Legion&quot; meets &quot;Pokemon&quot; work - and he did. Though the Pokemon aspects became more abstract than the original challenger may have intended.<br /> <br /> (this gets a little nuanced in-setting, as the city folk don't relate to their furies as individual entities, and their powers are as a result more reliable and elementally-diverse, but generally less powerful than what the &quot;paganoi&quot; country folk are capable of. The paganoi tend to have individual named furies, that often take specific animal forms out of their respective elements, and are more powerful but can have tempermental wills of their own. There are two opposing theories as to why this difference exists; the one most common among urban scholars is that it's of anthropomorphic origin. The paganoi are crafting their furies into distinct entities subconsciously. The most common theory among the paganoi is that the urban furies have been stripped of their idenities by the constant reworking of the environment. Point is that if varies how much the characters come off as just element-benders, or pokemon-summoners)<br /> <br /> One thing I'm really liking about the series (I'm on book 3) but am worried an eventual plot development is going to take away from me, is how in a setting where EVERYONE has magic, the one character without it seen as disabled in the social construct of the setting. It plays nicely with how disability is a social construct, and is a nice twist on the usual protagonist having super special powers making them the chosen one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I love Legend of Korra, but there is one and only one &quot;mediocre-to-bad&quot; episode of AtLA. That's the Great Divide. Literally every other episode is filled with narratively indespensible character development. I mean, there are some &quot;mediocre&quot; episodes relative to other AtLA episodes, but even those are miles above average kid's animated tv episodes.<br /> <br /> Korra suffers from the problem of its shorter format removed the ability for Korra to win one-off stories on her way to the big confrontations. Those &quot;filler&quot; conflicts were necessary to make the heroes still feel like they're competent and progressing while the villains are on the march. If the Fall of Bai Sing Se had been immediately followed by the Day of Black Sun, it would feel like the Gaang was constantly getting beaten down by their foes until they suddenly rise to deus ex machina victory in the finale - and that's what Legend of Korra often felt like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-30-2018, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:47:55-07:00","id":1201397,"title":"","content":"Never in my wildest dreams did I think the biggest criticism of What Fire Has Wrought would be me being tough on Legend of Korra. :P<br /> <br /> (which, I should be clear, I still love)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T13:50:13-07:00","id":1201399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201397#post1201397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never in my wildest dreams did I think the biggest criticism of What Fire Has Wrought would be me being tough on Legend of Korra. :P<br /> <br /> (which, I should be clear, I still love)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is always what you least expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T17:58:53-07:00","id":1201489,"title":"","content":"Time to resume our WIR with some more complaining about chapter fiction, wherein I reveal that I\u2019ve been cheating and actually already read the book once before starting to write down my impressions. Fair warning: this is going to be vicious.<br /> <br /> <br /> I genuinely hated this vignette. The <i>nicest thing</i> I can say about it is that it\u2019s likely to annoy the kind of people I don\u2019t like. When the biggest positive of the work is that it might make somebody\u2019s day more unpleasant, you know that it\u2019s\u2026 really not fantastic.<br /> <br /> (Still better than the worst of 2E chapter comics, though.)<br /> <br /> Okay, so why does it not work?<br /> <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s first summarize what happens, for those who don\u2019t have their own copy.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re at a gala. Our protagonist, the renowned merchant-adventurer Nellens Leferi, gets insulted by some rando who \u2013 unlike her \u2013 doesn\u2019t get his own entry under the description of his House. She responds in kind, and is attacked for her trouble. She proceeds to effortlessly whoop the ass of her opponent, then gloats about how this will earn her house new contracts for some reason.<br /> <br /> *Sigh.*<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably the most egregious problem is the weakness of the dialogue. The rest of the issues would be forgivable, if not for the fact that the writer apparently wants us to believe that lines such as <i>\u201eYou\u2019ve correctly identified my profession. Yet it seems your tutors were remiss in properly explaining how it works. Probably several tutors. Speaking slowly.\u201d </i>represent the height of wit.<br /> <br /> No, seriously, I can\u2019t emphasize enough how bad the dialogue is. The way it seems utterly divorced from how people actually talk and behave like. The young man\u2019s response to the line above? Shouting \u201eyou thin-blooded Nellens cur\u201d, and a roundhouse kick. Because clearly, \u201eyou\u2019re dim\u201d is the kind of hot diss that leaves no other recourse but to escalate to physical violence. At a party. In a society where patience and discipline are considered to be so important virtues that the stereotype of masculine intemperance seriously undermines the chances of men to be deemed suitable for higher leadership roles.<br /> <br /> Another example:<br /> \u201eYou dishonor yourself and your house with your clowning. I won\u2019t brook such insult to the name of Sesus\u2019 father\u201d \u2013 because apparently, launching into a tangent about the qualities a merchant must have is an insult to one\u2019s ancestors. Bhu\u2026 <i>what</i>? In what possible world does that make sense? (Let\u2019s, for a moment, ignore that a Sesus probably would not refer to Nellens as \u201eSesus\u2019 father\u201d. It\u2019s an ugly, clunky way to deliver exposition and context, but it pales in the face of the fact that whatever is coming out of Daral\u2019s mouth is just pure nonsense.)<br /> <br /> Yet another exchange:<br /> L: \u201cThe second thing a merchant learns is risk. You? Pretty, perhaps, but rash. Definitely low risk.\u201d<br /> D: \u201cFor the honor of my house!\u201d<br /> <br /> Daral\u2019s lines are embarrassing to even read. In and of itself, this wouldn\u2019t necessarily be a problem \u2013 he might just be the kind of person who is really bad at trash talk. That\u2019s a valid characterization! But the scene is bad and broken on multiple levels simultaneously in ways that mutually amplify the effect of each other.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the most important ways the writer fails at their intent? The framing of Sesus Daral. Giving him dialogue that befits a rash loudmouth who can\u2019t handle the bantz and prefers to let his fists do the talking is at odds with how he is being portrayed when his mouth isn\u2019t open.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201eSesus Daral fixed her with a cruel smirk, all muscle and chiseled features and swooning entourage.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201eThe young talonlord punctuated his remark with a dazzling and textbook-perfect spinning roundhouse.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> <i>\u201eLaughter came from the terrace above, though Daral silenced most of it with a glare.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> He\u2019s described as a person of some note (a military officer), surrounded by a \u201eswooning\u201d entourage, and apparently he has enough status among the guests that he can get most of them to stop laughing with a glare. The person that is being portrayed here is not somebody whose best idea of a comeback should be \u201eimma kick them in the face\u201d.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another problem is just how effortlessly he ends up being trounced. He heaves and strains and flares his anima, yet our protagonist vanquishes him without the slightest bit of exertion. The scene is devoid of any threat, and therefore tension; moreover, a hero is defined by the quality of her opposition, and successfully fighting a schoolyard bully who is a drooling dimwit and can\u2019t pose a meaningful physical challenge either is <i>not actually a good look</i>. I don\u2019t come away from reading the text with the impression that Leferi is awesome, I come away with the impression that Daral is really, really pathetic, and am left wondering why defeating such an unworthy foe would raise her status in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the scene kind of fails at setting up expectations and creating tension. You know what <i>else</i> it fails at? Maintaining basic consistency with the rest of the information contained within the book.<br /> <br /> What do we learn about the average member of House Sesus? \u201e<i>By the time a child learns to walk, she\u2019s started training in the games of Dynastic intrigue. Before entering primary school, she\u2019s studied the fundamentals of subterfuge and tradecraft.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> What do we learn about Nellens Leferi? \u201e<i>Nellens Leferi has carried out business transactions with petty Threshold despots, barbarian warlords, and the subterranean artificers of the Mountain Folk. When she\u2019s not adventuring throughout the Threshold and beyond in search of profitable ventures and trading partners, she acts as a proxy for the Conclave\u2019s commercial interests, putting both her business acumen and her formidable martial arts prowess to use bargaining with those too proud to palaver with mortals.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> It is clear that Daral is out there to start some shit. We also know that wearing house colors is not fashionable (\u201e<i>Every Great House also has a set of emblematic colors. Sometimes in vogue, their use is currently out of fashion. Today, wearing one\u2019s house colors \u2014 especially on a regular basis \u2014 is a sign of a traditionalist, though it\u2019s also a useful way to curry favor with elder Dynasts who might be a bit set in their ways.</i>\u201d). Yet he knows that the person he\u2019s insulting is a Nellens, and a merchant at that \u2013 so it stands to reason to assume that he did some legwork before coming to the party, maybe looked at a guest list and asked around about the names on it. <i>One</i> <i>would think maybe he could have learned that Leferi is known for her martial arts prowess, and looked for an easier target to bully</i>. So, I guess we can add \u201espying\u201d to the growing list of things Sesus Daral fails at.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the end of the day, the fundamental problem is that Daral is denied basic humanity. He is transparently not a person, but an obstacle to be thrown in the way of our hero and handily disposed of in a flash. We never learn why he thinks it\u2019s a good idea to start shit at a party. We never learn why his ego is so fragile that he immediately jumps to fisticuffs instead of trying to respond with an insult of his own (because let\u2019s face it, against the razor wit displayed by Leferi, even a \u201eno u\u201d would suffice). We never learn how he could fail so badly at the basic shtick of the House he is so proudly a part of.<br /> <br /> This would be forgivable if the scene was entertainingly written. It isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026I think this is enough words about what I didn\u2019t like. Next time, we\u2019ll be back with the cool stuff! Maybe even look at Cathak. We\u2019ll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T19:00:16-07:00","id":1201502,"title":"","content":"I could see Daral's judgement being impaired by the House's particular hatred for Nellens. Either that, or he's one of those Sesus that is said to wash out of the spy training, and lives in more of the overt martial and social personas of the House.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf I find nothing wrong with the dialogue, perhaps that's because I expect the formality and ritual of Dynasts to sound like that.<br /> <br /> Considering how short these fictions are, and the kind of power that the Exalted can have, I think it's okay for there to be plenty of them that are about demonstrating prowess rather than building tension.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T19:21:00-07:00","id":1201505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201502#post1201502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIf I find nothing wrong with the dialogue, perhaps that's because I expect the formality and ritual of Dynasts to sound like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's a duel of wits that is woefully short on wit, and more importantly, the dialogue isn't an actual dialogue - the characters just make exclamations in the vague direction of each other, without bothering to react to anything the other party says.<br /> <br /> (Sorry if this sounds terse. I just really don't have it in me to put any more effort into the subject - in my teens, I took great pleasure in eviscerating the things I didn't like in exacting detail, but after typing up the previous post, I mostly just felt embarrassment at having spewed three pages of venom about a really tiny aspect of a game that I otherwise like and at having wasted three hours of my life giving attention to something I explicitly did not enjoy. Funny how an activity that used to be cathartic at one point in my life nowadays just makes me feel like a sucker.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 03-30-2018, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T21:09:27-07:00","id":1201533,"title":"","content":"The line about dishonoring yourself with your clowning, I assumed was him responding to the fact that she was just dodging, refusing to fight, instead of actually engaging him.<br /> <br /> Also, if you look at it as a story or parable where &quot;Intemperate Man loses his wits, allowing Clear Headed Woman to one up him&quot; it might work better? I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T19:43:31-07:00","id":1201815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201262#post1201262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Some would no doubt say that this is <b>retarded</b>, because in an alternate universe where Sabriye the gutter rat is not <i>also</i> Sabriye the Solar Exalt, the same confrontation would end up with her skewered on the point of a spear. To this, I can only respond with \u201eyou\u2019re missing the point\u201d.)</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bDo you really need to be told not to use the word retarded like this? Don't do it again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T14:40:02-07:00","id":1202024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1201533#post1201533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The line about dishonoring yourself with your clowning, I assumed was him responding to the fact that she was just dodging, refusing to fight, instead of actually engaging him.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My problem with that interpretation is that it requires us to assume that Daral has <i>no self-awareness whatsoever</i>, adding even more things to the list of what he's terrible at. This wouldn\u2019t be a problem in and of itself (\u201elack of self-awareness\u201d sounds like a go-to flaw for a typical Dynast), but he\u2019s already very difficult to take seriously \u2013 and again, him being generally bad at everything cheapens Leferi\u2019s victory.<br /> <br /> But speaking of self-awareness, I realize that any more complaining about the fiction would veer suspiciously close to &quot;what about the menz?&quot; hand-wringing, so let's drop the subject and proceed with the rest of chapter 2.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have no particularly valuable insight about most of the information we\u2019re given before we get to the House descriptions, save for two things.<br /> <br /> One that I think underlines the point that game mechanics don\u2019t necessarily correspond to in-setting reality is the following: \u201e<i>The house\u2019s hearthstones and artifacts are likewise the matriarch\u2019s to apportion. However, bonding with artifacts takes time and a compatible disposition. Once a loyal scion awakens an heirloom\u2019s Evocations, the matriarch typically allows him to retain it for as long as it\u2019s of use to him.</i>\u201d This is interesting to me, because a lot \u2013 if not the overwhelming majority \u2013 of artifacts in Arms of the Chosen immediately unlock their first Evocation for any non-dissonant wielder upon attunement. Here, we\u2019re shown that this is actually an abstraction of what happens (all in all, a pretty good concession, because fuck having to track an arbitrary amount of time before a character is allowed to grab an Evocation they\u2019re getting for free).<br /> <br /> Another thing is the House colors \u2013 some of these combinations are staggeringly ugly (V\u2019neef\u2019s green and purple takes the cake, but the Nellens brown and silver is also pretty bad). Note that the Houses with the worst color schemes are the ones with the least amount of prestige. Also: V\u2019neef herself is characterized as \u201ea charismatic and dignified woman with the Empress\u2019 social savvy and beauty\u201d \u2013 in other words, a probable trend-setter in Dynastic society. Wearing House colors is out of fashion now. Coincidence? I think not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T16:41:41-07:00","id":1202051,"title":"","content":"I think it was referring to the suite as a whole. The evocations you get up front are stuff the magic sword just does, and probably wouldn't count. <br /> <br /> Basically they let you keep stuff you've actually invested exp in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:27:00-07:00","id":1202107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202024#post1202024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing is the House colors \u2013 some of these combinations are staggeringly ugly (V\u2019neef\u2019s green and purple takes the cake, but the Nellens brown and silver is also pretty bad). Note that the Houses with the worst color schemes are the ones with the least amount of prestige. Also: V\u2019neef herself is characterized as \u201ea charismatic and dignified woman with the Empress\u2019 social savvy and beauty\u201d \u2013 in other words, a probable trend-setter in Dynastic society. Wearing House colors is out of fashion now. Coincidence? I think not.</div> </div> </div> </div>That House colors are out of fashion felt strangely out of place to me. I would have expected that section to note wearing family colors came back into fashion with the disappearance of the Empress and the Great Houses asserting dominance over the organs of the Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1564-shinjo","name":"Shinjo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T19:55:28-07:00","id":1202110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shinjo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202107#post1202107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That House colors are out of fashion felt strangely out of place to me. I would have expected that section to note wearing family colors came back into fashion with the disappearance of the Empress and the Great Houses asserting dominance over the organs of the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a purposeful kind of trying to avoid the Great Houses looking like the L5R clans and having some utlity in the idea that the folks who do use house colors are nerds or suck-ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:03:48-07:00","id":1202184,"title":"","content":"I'd expect them to use the house colours for the uniforms of their armies if they end up going to war on each other. <br /> <br /> Team colours are useful in certain situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T04:20:06-07:00","id":1202192,"title":"","content":"<b>Cathak \u2014 Fire That Marches Against the Tide</b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026An \u201einteresting\u201d inversion of Kimbery\u2019s sobriquet, that\u2019s for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> In a nutshell, they\u2019re militaristic, honorable and devout. Kind of vanilla, but you know what? <i>Vanilla is actually a rich and complex flavor.</i> Nothing wrong with vanilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, apparently Gateway was invented by a Cathak. You learn something new every day!<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no idea how battlefield tactics and stratagems are supposed to translate to political maneuvering. Oh god please don\u2019t tell me their courtiers are like those insufferable managerial types who think reading <i>The Book of Five Circles</i> and <i>The Art of War</i> has prepared them for every eventuality.<br /> <br /> (\u2026Probably not. I imagine Cathak scions are many things, but \u201ewannabe\u201d is not one of them.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay this is actually my favorite quote in the entire book:<br /> \u201e<i>House Cathak strongly encourages daughters to join the military. This creates a need for husbands skilled in finance, administration, and the like. Cathak marriage negotiations are tense affairs, but because they value skill over status and pedigree, they offer lowborn sons of Dynastic families fallen on hard times the hope of improving their station. Such marriages are thought to be warmer and more passionate than most, contributing to the starry-eyed way in which many young male Dynasts dream of marrying into this house. Poetry and romances about the impoverished son of a falling branch being swept off his feet by a Cathak officer of wide experience and taken off to a life of luxury and adventure are popular.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but imagine that at <i>any</i> given point in time during the school year, there is at least one nerdy-looking accountant guy in the Spiral Academy looking out on the window and daydreaming about an impossibly perfect military waifu who will magically help him turn his life around and transform it into the awesome adventure he always thought he deserved to live.<br /> <br /> I also can\u2019t help but imagine that a vanishingly few see those fantasies turned into reality, and <i>fucking hate it</i>. (Awesome military adventures are considerably less awesome when you have the chiseled physique of the average accountant.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I love the expression \u201ethe dragon\u2019s share\u201d, even though it gets overused in this chapter. The reason I like it is that it works on <i>three</i> levels at the same time: out of setting, it works because dragons have been associated with greed ever since Fafnir, so it\u2019s immediately obvious what it refers to; in setting, it works in places where Immaculates hold sway, since the Dragon-Blooded are at the top of the Perfected Hierarchy and the bounty of Creation belongs to them; and it works in the Threshold as well, because so much wealth is flowing into the Realm that \u201ea portion that\u2019s about the size of the part of our economy that these assholes are taking away\u201d can credibly work out to mean the majority of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>The legions also fatten House Cathak\u2019s coffers by providing escort services for goods and personnel throughout the Threshold, exacting fees that, while far smaller than what House V\u2019neef earns from escorting tribute shipments, are nevertheless significant. The house usually has a few such assignments in progress at any time, and they provide an excellent excuse for a young Cathak to see Creation.</i>\u201d \u2013 I like this part, it serves as an excellent hook for a group where every character comes from the same House. (Which I prefer. Few things kill my fun both as a GM and a player as quickly as a group that tears itself apart in internal conflict.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Others have already pointed out that the Cathak strategy of profiting for the impeding civil war is pretty ingenious, but I guess I\u2019ll add my voice to the chorus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the House\u2019s holdings, it\u2019s interesting that they\u2019ve got Harborhead, but more interesting is Fajad. The awesome preview paints a very vivid picture, and one that is very gameplay-friendly (as opposed to redolent with details a GM could just improvise on the spot \u2013 a mistake many setting books make). It would serve well as a homebase for the Cathak escort campaign concept floated above, with the political situation deteriorating even further between adventures until things come to a head.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of note!<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Cathak was also a famed ascetic plagued by doubt and dark thoughts, spending months in seclusion writing military treatises and contemplating spiritual matters, then emerging for days of wild debauchery</i>\u201d \u2013 yeah, that sounds like a distinctly Fire Aspect approach to asceticism. I like it.<br /> <br /> \u2026Wait, we\u2019re getting <i>stats</i> for Cathak Cainan? Awesome.<br /> <br /> Garel feels like the essence of House Cathak distilled in one person. She\u2019ll make a fine matriarch.<br /> <br /> I bet Elanda has the Giant merit. It\u2019s weird that we\u2019re <i>not</i> getting stats for her, because she would be a good opportunity to showcase how a build that foregoes Dex in favor of Strength can be effective on its own right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T05:45:02-07:00","id":1202201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202192#post1202192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve no idea how battlefield tactics and stratagems are supposed to translate to political maneuvering. Oh god please don\u2019t tell me their courtiers are like those insufferable managerial types who think reading <i>The Book of Five Circles</i> and <i>The Art of War</i> has prepared them for every eventuality.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bFor every eventuality, sure, but The Art of War is mostly about cultivating a mindset of assessing one's resources and recognising and seizing opportunities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also can\u2019t help but imagine that a vanishingly few see those fantasies turned into reality, and <i>fucking hate it</i>. (Awesome military adventures are considerably less awesome when you have the chiseled physique of the average accountant.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, Lore allows them to shoot elemental bolts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI agree that Cathak is still the least interesting House to me, but the overall bar has been raised to the degree that I still find it very vivid and powerful. Things like them having a general enthusiasm for competition and being marked as the single strongest military power in the Realm help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T15:15:23-07:00","id":1202315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202201#post1202201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell, Lore allows them to shoot elemental bolts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, it won't help them march for days, nor will it make the experience of sleeping in a ditch any more pleasant, so the main problems remain. Poor, poor Spiral Academy graduates.<br /> <br /> <br /> And our next House is\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Cynis \u2014 Wood Nourished On Tears of The Fallen</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/016/925/498ed76be651cffb6bb9bac6a9bb75c3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Actually, \u201ewood nourished on tears\u201d sounds exactly like the kind of kinky I\u2019d imagine a Cynis scion to get up to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like that they seem to be a genuinely popular House now, instead of the creepy kids everybody visits because hey, free drugs, but nobody actually <i>likes</i>. (Which is the impression I\u2019ve got from their earlier incarnations.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Interesting that three out of the ten major Houses seem to have spying as a major focus \u2013 and they\u2019re all different kinds of spying, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026So apparently medicine joins prostitution, slaves and drugs as one of the pillars of their economy. Yeah, I guess it fits them.<br /> <br /> <br /> There\u2019s an interesting point being made about the Cynis information advantage and the difficulties in actually turning that advantage into tangible influence, lemme get a quote:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Those who\u2019ve accepted Cynis hospitality \u2014 and there are few who haven\u2019t \u2014 know that the Cynis reputation for discretion is well earned. No matter how great the improprieties committed at a Cynis gala, a Dynast may rest easy knowing that her reputation is safe. Of course, House Cynis, watches, reports, and records. There\u2019s no piece of information too small to be used. </i><br /> <i>Using this information, however, is an option of last resort. Release news of a scandal too publicly and no one will ever let loose at a Cynis celebration again. There\u2019s no way to tell how the information will spread once released, so most play their cards close to their chest and work through insinuation. But if a particular political rival needs to be burned, a Cynis scion might mention something to an Immaculate monk, who\u2019ll discreetly censure the blackmailed party while leaving House Cynis blameless of any breach of hospitality.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Now, the part that is unclear to me is why would the Immaculates \u2013 who are noted to harbor serious misgivings about House Cynis in general \u2013 trust <i>any</i> of the information they\u2019re given this way. It\u2019s not like it could be corroborated with audio recordings or video evidence. Ah well.<br /> <br /> (\u2026I mean, a courtier who can\u2019t subtly plant the idea into the head of an Immaculate who spent most of his time improving his martial arts prowess at the expense of delicate social maneuvering must be really bad at her job.)<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Experimenting with Creation\u2019s flora and fauna in search of the next high or cure has given House Cynis an unparalleled knowledge of toxins, venoms, and other deadly substances. Many compounds in the house vaults cannot be replicated without their massive trade network, nor can their antidotes. House Cynis discreetly offers these poisons to Dynasts and criminals willing to pay, and uses its extensive information-gathering network to ascertain the victim\u2019s identity to determine their next step. If it\u2019s someone the house wants gone, nothing further needs doing, and they\u2019ve been paid for the privilege of having an enemy assassinated. If they\u2019d rather see him live, they arrange for him to meet a Cynis physician, who\u2019ll cluck her tongue and talk of summer fevers or winter chills while administering antidotes made from ingredients plucked from gardens and grottoes thousands of miles away. The value of the patient\u2019s gratitude is equaled only by the steep cost charged for the service.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> Yeah, getting paid twice for the same end result as not doing anything seems like a very Cynis approach to work. I approve.<br /> <br /> <br /> To the surprise of nobody, Cynis and Sesus are really closely intertwined. Screw stories of starry-eyed Spiral Academy graduates and dashing Cathak heroines, what I want now is a romance between a Cynis courtier and a Sesus spy.<br /> <br /> I imagine Realm literature has ample examples: syrupy takes on the redemptive power of friendship and love, probably featuring unlikely circumstances in which the star-crossed lovers form a Sworn Kinship with an overly earnest Earth Aspect and a passionate Fire Aspect who teach them the value of honesty and opening up emotionally. Heart-wrenching generational epics where personal feelings must be sacrificed on the altar of House politics, betrayals great and small abound, and with the passing of centuries, the relationship turns more and more antagonistic, with things eventually coming to a head in a spectacular kung fu battle between elder Exalts (tragic reconciliation as one party succumbs to their injuries is optional, but common). Thinly-veiled Immaculate morality tales in which unchecked lust and impiety lead the lovers down a dark path of consorting with demons and blasphemous Anathema, which end with one of them consumed by their twisted desires but the other finding the strength to repent, turn against their new blasphemous masters, and earn redemption in death. And, of course, just plain old porn (albeit \u201edebauched Cynis leads a naive Cathak into a world of new experiences\u201d is probably a more widespread subgenre there by a wide margin).<br /> <br /> I also imagine the relationships portrayed in these are nothing like the real thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Holdings are not very interesting \u2013 I imagine Pangu will work out pretty well when The Realm drops, but it\u2019s hard to do miracles in two paragraphs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of note!<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>A trailblazing explorer, master merchant, and inveterate hedonist, <b>Cynis </b>herself died centuries ago of an overdose of heroin laced with dreamstone dust.</i>\u201d \u2013 I adore this. If I was a Dynast, I\u2019d want to be like Cynis when I grow up. (Not even on regular heroin! It\u2019s extra-super-special-bad-for-you heroin that may or may not have had Wyld stuff added to it. <i>I have no idea what dreamstone dust is but it sounds awesome</i>.)<br /> <br /> I have to admit, the way Cynis Wisel is described here annoys me slightly. We can\u2019t have a character who is <i>just</i> a talented poet; no, somebody who cannot inflict horrendous violence on others is apparently not worth mentioning :P<br /> <br /> Petalin is an interesting one, because the text frames her as a candidate for the throne, but she\u2026 doesn\u2019t seem to be a very effective leader? She\u2019s popular among the troops, but apparently hasn\u2019t really managed to improve the quality of the house legions since she was put into a leadership position. (Maybe it happened recently?)<br /> <br /> I enjoy the idea that loving one\u2019s husband causes an <i>image problem</i> among the Cynis, and therefore it must be prevented from becoming public knowledge. Probably not what the writer was thinking of, but I enjoy it nonetheless.<br /> <br /> \u2026Wait, souls can <i>go missing</i>? How does that even happen? (I mean, one way is obvious, but there is explicitly no coming back from that one \u2013 albeit I guess the text doesn\u2019t say that Umara is going to put back the original one\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T18:10:30-07:00","id":1202379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202315#post1202315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the part that is unclear to me is why would the Immaculates \u2013 who are noted to harbor serious misgivings about House Cynis in general \u2013 trust <i>any</i> of the information they\u2019re given this way. It\u2019s not like it could be corroborated with audio recordings or video evidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how serious you're being here. <br /> <br /> Like, if I were to tell an authority figure, &quot;I saw Alice strangle an eight-year-old,&quot; I don't think there's any point in history where the authority figure would just tell me to come back next time with some video of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:09:41-07:00","id":1202414,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine Cynis is decently good at making sure they keep some form of record or evidence in the event that the material might stretch their credibility. Otherwise I'd presume probably a mix of proxies passing along the information, you know the concerned servant slipping under their master's notice to inform on problematic behavior, or just the old fashioned method of having people who do generally trust you, or know that there are circumstances where you're not going to attempt to mislead them and keep those sacrosanct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T14:48:11-07:00","id":1202744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202379#post1202379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how serious you're being here.<br /> <br /> Like, if I were to tell an authority figure, &quot;I saw Alice strangle an eight-year-old,&quot; I don't think there's any point in history where the authority figure would just tell me to come back next time with some video of it.</div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> I\u2026 genuinely don\u2019t think most Dynastic blackmail material is quite the same magnitude as strangling children, though? I imagine most of it is something to the effect of \u201eI happened to overhear Alice bragging to Bob about how skillfully she managed to embezzle something or subvert the Imperial justice system\u201d, which... you <i>could</i> report to the Immaculates, who will eventually prompt the authorities into launching an investigation and uncovering evidence of misdeeds (or, at least, forcing Alice to waste a bunch of her time and money on trying to obstruct the process and issue extravagant bribes), but it feels like there\u2019s a superfluous extra step involved there. Especially considering that the IO is packed to the brim with people who are loyal to Cynis\u2019 greatest enemy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ledaal \u2014 Air that Raised the Bones of Giants</b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Yeah I have no idea what that is supposed to mean either.<br /> <br /> <br /> So House Ledaal is basically the Holy Inquisition of the God-Empress of Mankind. I\u2026 can live with that, and even see how that is compelling, but after having spent an overwhelming majority of my time as a roleplayer either running or playing in W40K, I can\u2019t say that it makes me particularly enthused about them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, they\u2019re not even trying to get on the throne. Honestly, I feel like this is the strategy Cynis should\u2019ve chosen as well \u2013 I imagine a lot of their current trouble with Mnemon would simply not be present had they not gone and pissed her off by running against her.<br /> <br /> \u2026I mean, you could argue that a devout Mnemon on the throne would be pretty bad for their business, but I can\u2019t really imagine her being in a position to strongarm a House that has conserved its power throughout the civil war just after the dust has settled and everybody is licking their wounds. Also, I imagine she\u2019d move against V\u2019neef just out of sheer pettiness, which would give Cynis the opportunity to muscle in on their turf and shift their image to a more restrained and doctrinally acceptable one.<br /> <br /> <br /> But enough about Cynis, this is the time for discussing Ledaal! (Favoritism? What do you mean favoritism?)<br /> <br /> <br /> Interesting \u2013 two out of the three founders we\u2019ve seen so far have been adopted by the Empress.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, they seem to have the Crab shtick of desperately trying to call attention to the massive existential threats next door while everybody around them is content to play petty politics.<br /> <br /> <br /> House Ledaal\u2019s approach to their satrapies seems like a rich vein to mine for conflict:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Many households reside in the Threshold, soaking up local culture and bringing back wealth and craftsmanship. It doesn\u2019t endear them to the locals, though \u2014tributaries under Ledaal\u2019s thumb know they represent nothing more than a resource and a staging ground for the Shadow Crusade. Constant vigilance against the rising dark makes Ledaal satrapies among the safest places for citizens of the Threshold to live, but in exchange they sacrifice privacy and autonomy. The yoke of Imperial oversight grows heavier as the house scours its holdings for Anathema sympathies, and demands increasing resources to shore up its grip on Arjuf and fund Wyld Hunts.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> On one hand, you can see the growing frustration of the Ledaal, desperate to help as their family members are getting maimed and killed fighting against Anathema and other threats with each passing day, and viewing the locals as ungrateful little bastards who don\u2019t even have the <i>capacity</i> to appreciate what the House is doing for them, because it\u2019s so far removed from their experience. On the other hand, you have the misery of the common folk who see their country gutted and bled for every obol just so that their Dragon-Blooded overlords can wage war against threats thousands of miles away \u2013 and sure, dying to the Fair Folk and the hungry dead ain\u2019t pleasant, but neither is starving in the winter because tax collectors took away the last of your grain, not to mention that if the wealth of their country wasn\u2019t siphoned away into Ledaal coffers for centuries, maybe they could\u2019ve put up some meaningful defenses of their own already. Then you have the PCs decide which viewpoint has more validity in their eyes. Good stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like how their position manages to be strong yet precarious at the same time, both in military and politics.<br /> <br /> <br /> House holdings!<br /> <br /> <br /> So Howling Heart Prefecture has the following: \u201e<i>Through sorcery and reverse-engineering ancient artifacts of Anathema make, they\u2019ve developed a still-theoretical protocol to dramatically amplify a Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence for a short period, at the cost of major decreases in lifespan and blood purity. They haven\u2019t deployed it yet, for it carries the risk of inciting Essence fever nigh unto madness, but the resurgence of the Solar Anathema may force their hand</i>\u201d. I\u2019ve got to say, I\u2019m not a fan. This feels like a cheap way to provide \u201elevel-appropriate combat challenge\u201d to rapidly developing Solars without breaking the setting in half by suddenly revealing elder Exalts in every corner. I\u2019m <i>especially</i> not a fan of it having a good chance to turn the affected into ravening madmen, because the one thing worse for Exalted than having NPCs whose narrative role begins and ends with \u201eappropriate combat challenge for high xp solars\u201d is implicitly saying \u201eand it\u2019s morally okay to put them down, they\u2019re mentally unstable, violent lunatics anyway\u201d.<br /> <br /> (Funnily enough, they would actually be fine antagonists in an Infernal game, underlining a point about tearing away your humanity bit by bit on a quest for Real Ultimate Power<sup>TM</sup>.)<br /> <br /> (Also: this is <i>one</i> reading of the passage in question. It\u2019s entirely possible to interpret it in a considerably less negative light! My issue is that the reading which would result in clich\u00e9 and lazy storytelling is a very obvious one. Reminder: \u201ethe Yozis escape from Hell\u201d was a popular campaign event even back in 1E despite the fact that the book explicitly called it out as impossible.)<br /> <br /> (\u2026Man it feels weird to rail against badwrongfun just a page after having said that there is a tendency in the fan community to focus on internal consistency and setting minutiae to a degree where it shuts down play instead of enabling stories.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll just quote this in its entirety without comment because it\u2019s awesome:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>The city-state <b>Perch</b>, in the Southern land of Zephyr, sprawls along the east bank of the Elidad River, whose rich soil yields fine harvests. But the west bank hosts only the Twilight Grove, Perch\u2019s shadowland necropolis. There, the dead keep their hearts close at hand to better recall the passions of life, and spectral princes called aeons ride sphinxes that are their own hungry ghosts. The satrap, Ledaal Yasmet Imara, treats as an equal with the seven archaeons that rule the dead city, bargaining for occult secrets and Underworld gossip. Other than burial rites, she forbids intercourse between the two cities, but turns a blind eye to the many little flowerings of Perch\u2019s ancestor cult. Though she\u2019d love to extirpate the cult root and branch, Perch has seen too many uprisings in the past, and Imara does not dare tempt another at this delicate time.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of note!<br /> <br /> \u2026I will never cease to adore the term \u201emasculine intemperance\u201d.<br /> <br /> Ledaal Kebok Coren is interesting. How does somebody get a demon great-granddaddy in a House of demon hunters? Also: custom Charms can be used reflect extraordinary heritage now? I thought the Exaltation burned such things away in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T15:52:11-07:00","id":1202776,"title":"","content":"Ledaal Kebok Coren has been a demon-blooded dragon-blood with magic demon storm powers since the 1e DB hardcover; material that claimed things like &quot;You can't be a demon-blooded dragon-blood with magic demon storm powers because Exaltation burns those away!&quot; post-dates her, and seems largely to have been written by people with oWoD experience who thought it was their job to stomp down on vampire-werewolf hybrid abominations and the munchkins who want to play them. This is Exalted, though, and Ledaal Kebok Coren has always been cool, so we're running with her.<br /> <br /> (A given Exalt's powers are already so diverse there's no real harm in letting someone diversify a bit more, provided they're paying XP for the Charms. Also, &quot;I make it storm when I'm angry&quot; isn't super game-breaking.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:00:28-07:00","id":1202782,"title":"","content":"Is playing a character like Coren something that will get wordcount when you get around God-Blooded? Or is it more of a play it by ear thing, where it's just &quot;special circumstance lets the character wield a very narrow selection of custom designed spirit Charms as would be available for Eclipse Keyword&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T16:15:50-07:00","id":1202786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202782#post1202782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is playing a character like Coren something that will get wordcount when you get around God-Blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, definitely. If the God-Blooded rules don't let you play Ledaal Kebok Coren, then the God-Blooded rules are wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T04:31:52-07:00","id":1202946,"title":"","content":"<b>Mnemon \u2014 Earth Carved in the Image of One</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Immediately in the second paragraph, we\u2019re given a very good reason why we\u2019d want to play one:<br /> <br /> \u201e<i>A slim majority of scions receive Immaculate training at the Cloister of Wisdom. But while some grow rigid in their piety, others study at far-flung Threshold temples and cities, exposing them to many of Creation\u2019s most outlandish and enthralling aesthetics, cultures, and spiritual paths. As a result, they have a distinct flair of exoticism bordering on salacious, and a wisdom bordering on heretical.</i>\u201d<br /> <br /> This is good stuff. \u201eThe devout House\u201d is a pretty narrow niche. However, the contrast between being an exemplar of Dynastic values and someone with a foreign outlook and insights, that is a rich vein to mine for character concepts. Oh, and you get to know magic kung fu. <i>Awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Was the House always so focused on construction? I don\u2019t seem to recall that from earlier editions.<br /> <br /> <br /> When your allies include the biggest naval power and the House with the strongest legions, everybody else being against you doesn\u2019t seem too bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> Paragon is surprisingly conflict-free.<br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, Isator Levi has already said all there is to say about the Inner Circle and Mnemon\u2019s character.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>If only the rest of the Dynasty wanted another Scarlet Empress, she\u2019d sit upon the throne right now</i>\u201d \u2013 that\u2019s a pretty good line, and I think it summarizes the Dynasty\u2019s relationship with Her Redness succintly.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like Rulinsei\u2019s characterization as a \u201emiddling\u201d sorcerer. Not every elder Exalt needs to be an omnicompetent, transcendent genius. Sometimes, being \u201ejust\u201d a master geomancer is <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like how Pallan\u2019s writeup manages to sneak in some setting details about the perception of infidelity \u2013 albeit this is elaborated on to hilarious effect in a later chapter. (Apparently husbands whose infidelity is known to have resulted in an unwanted pregnancy sometimes have a valet assigned to them indefinitely, with the sole purpose of carrying around maiden tea and reminding them to take it. I love this.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Mnemon Rulinsei Ghova is possibly my favorite NPC in the entire book, and his shtick will never cease to be a chasing the dragon pun for me (no matter how much Minton insists to the contrary). He\u2019s a very <i>conceptually dense</i> character, possibly serving as a source for a character\u2019s cool bling with unique aesthetics, illustrating the effects of Wyld exposure, dropping not one but <i>two</i> plot hooks (I don\u2019t know what \u201ethe irreal Noumenon\u201d is but it\u2019s cool-sounding enough to jumpstart a GM\u2019s imagination), and describing an awesome heresy while subtly implying that <i>your</i> Mnemon could have similarly outlandish interpretations of the Immaculate Philosophy without facing overt censure for that. If only every NPC writeup in the book could accomplish this much in a single paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 04-04-2018, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T07:22:37-07:00","id":1202993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202946#post1202946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know what \u201ethe irreal Noumenon\u201d is but it\u2019s cool-sounding enough to jumpstart a GM\u2019s imagination</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSuddenly it sounded vaguely familiar to me... something to do with a wasp? Is it an obscure reference to something of Jenna Moran's? Or am I just thinking that because it sounds vaguely like &quot;ichneumon&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T07:29:43-07:00","id":1202994,"title":"","content":"Mnemon being the architect house is new this edition I think. The house didn't really have an economic gimick as much as I can remember in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:58:52-07:00","id":1203030,"title":"","content":"I really liked the way all the houses got given a specific responsibility by the Empress. It explains their specialisations more.<br /> <br /> There was some of this before, but 3rd ed has made it a bigger thing. And giving nobles monopolies over particular areas was a common economic system in the pre-modern and early modern periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-04-2018, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T09:10:44-07:00","id":1203036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1203030#post1203030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And giving nobles monopolies over particular areas was a common economic system in the pre-modern and early modern periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still is on most countries today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T14:31:03-07:00","id":1203140,"title":"","content":"<b>Nellens \u2014 Dragons of the Blood Resurgent</b><br /> <br /> <br /> From a player perspective, Nellens strikes me as a bit of a superfluous House \u2013 you want to play the underdog but at the same time also want to have the backing of and the status of belonging to a Great House? Those seem like contradictory goals. You\u2019d probably get a more credible underdog story out of playing a Dragon-Blooded patrician or a cadet house member.<br /> <br /> \u2026I guess you could say that they make a pretty good House for Dynasts who Exalt as something other than a Dragon-Blooded, but I think that this is a misleading impression. Half the fun of playing a mortal-Dynast-turned-Celestial is being a terrible disappointment to your dear family, which you can\u2019t really be in a House where un-Exalted members are largely accepted.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Actually, the Nellens scion who washed out of secondary school and had to finish her education at a lesser academy, treated as a thin-blooded mongrel by her Dynastic peers and as a failure who squandered her potential despite having an advantage for which most of her siblings would\u2019ve given an arm and leg by her House, and has to make do with wits, ingenuity, and a wealth of connections among lowly mortal functionaries is a pretty damn compelling character concept, come to think of it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Diverse portfolio, financially stable, weak military, great connections. Gotcha. Others have pretty much said everything there is to say about these aspects.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Wow, they have a lot of enemies for a House with supposedly great connections.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not much in the way of territories. Sad, because this means fewer chronicle hooks. Ah well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of note!<br /> <br /> Nellens Sabine is described inconsistently \u2013 in the general House writeup, she is characterized as \u201e<i>a young mortal sorcerer who oversees the house\u2019s matchmaking efforts</i>\u201d, whereas her personal writeup says she\u2019s in her sixties. That\u2019s young for an Exalt, but she\u2019s a mortal!<br /> <br /> Leferi could be a cool mentor figure for an Exigent campaign, I guess.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I\u2019m more weirded out by the fact that a bureau tasked with standardizing measures across the Realm has been depicted as a joke for two editions than by the fact that someone belonging to it is getting useful leverage out of it. Standardized measures are really important!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T14:36:55-07:00","id":1203141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1203140#post1203140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nellens Sabine is described inconsistently \u2013 in the general House writeup, she is characterized as \u201e<i>a young mortal sorcerer who oversees the house\u2019s matchmaking efforts</i>\u201d, whereas her personal writeup says she\u2019s in her sixties. That\u2019s young for an Exalt, but she\u2019s a mortal!</div> </div> </div> </div>And a sorcerer, mind you. Given the availability of anagathics in the Realm and the ability of sorcerous workings to extend the user's life, I'd say that sixty can still be considered &quot;on the young side.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T16:40:12-07:00","id":1203178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1203030#post1203030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really liked the way all the houses got given a specific responsibility by the Empress. It explains their specialisations more.<br /> <br /> There was some of this before, but 3rd ed has made it a bigger thing. And giving nobles monopolies over particular areas was a common economic system in the pre-modern and early modern periods.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSomething that really made it click for me was how, just a few days before the book dropped, I happened upon articles about the ancient Greek institutions of the phyle and phratry, and the Baradari groups of India. It's why I've been describing Great Houses as feeling less like extended families of aristocrats and more like tribal entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1203140#post1203140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I\u2019m more weirded out by the fact that a bureau tasked with standardizing measures across the Realm has been depicted as a joke for two editions than by the fact that someone belonging to it is getting useful leverage out of it. Standardized measures are really important!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI believe that the joke there was that it was a fairly mundane and unglamourous ministry, given a particularly flowery and overwrought name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T16:14:43-07:00","id":1204330,"title":"","content":"<b>Peleps \u2014 Water That Wreaths the Crown of Centuries</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Dashing adventurers. Exemplars of Dynastic virtue. Yeah, they\u2019re not going be my favorite House.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>\u2019The trade winds\u2019 is a Peleps idiom for the vagaries of fate, and it\u2019s commonly accepted that the results of luck are well-earned \u2014 to be foiled by the trade winds is a sign of unworthiness, while taking unexpected advantage of them is lauded.</i>\u201d \u2013 something something bootstraps. They\u2019re <i>definitely</i> not going to be my favorite House, this much is for certain.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Admiralty Board is cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> Between the squeezing of satrapies and the indiscriminate raids on \u201epirate\u201d ships, I expect they\u2019re gonna be a major driver of conflict for non-DB games. This is a good thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> (I imagine their current position is akin to that of a Stellaris player who was already stretching the limits of their naval capacity, then lost a system that served as a major source of income and capacity, and suddenly OH MY GOD EVERYTHING IS FLASHING RED.)<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026A Western Empire, huh? I like that not every House\u2019s endgame revolves around the Scarlet Throne anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>Almost all admirals are Peleps women. Dragon-Blooded rise higher and faster than anyone else, and they enjoy more leeway than their mortal colleagues, but when they do fall, they fall harder and faster. A disgraced Dragon-Blooded officer is often shunted none-too-gently into some other profession where he can be useful without being seen.</i>\u201d \u2013 Some other profession like\u2026 what, exactly? Paper pushing? It\u2019s not like they used to have House legions before, and a career in the military is hardly a place where one is not being seen. (Funnily enough, Bureaucracy is a Water aspect ability. Now there\u2019s a character concept, \u201efailed captain turned economic advisor to her Cathak wife\u201d.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Much like in the Cynis writeup about blackmail, the book reinforces the idea that great power must be wielded delicately. Brute force solutions rarely yield favorable outcomes. This is very consistent with the core premise behind Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure what right Peleps has to feel disgust towards Nellens; it\u2019s not like their blood is particularly pure either, with Mnemon specifically mentioned to shun marriages with them for that reason. I\u2019d have expected that snobbery from a House with better pedigree.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201e<i>House Tepet once had House Peleps\u2019 deepest respect; now, the opinion among Peleps scions is that Tepet has shown weakness and should have the decency to die quickly. Then they can eulogize the fallen house, remembering its greatness, instead of having it hang onto the Realm like a lamprey.</i>\u201d \u2013 \u201eHurry on with the dying so we can say our tearful goodbyes\u201d sounds like a very Peleps attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026Sesus really likes antagonizing <i>everybody</i>, don\u2019t they?<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand others have pretty much said everything there is to say about the scions of note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T17:41:42-07:00","id":1204354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1204330#post1204330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what right Peleps has to feel disgust towards Nellens; it\u2019s not like their blood is particularly pure either, with Mnemon specifically mentioned to shun marriages with them for that reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though that comment was more about Mnemon's unusually high standards, rather then Peleps having a particular problem. The House Mnemon write-up had noted the exacting standards earlier on, and the significance of the relationship to Peleps strikes me as an instance in which it is something that is hamstringing them when it's sabotaging the opportunity for a highly beneficial alliance.<br /> <br /> \u200bI mean, Peleps obviously has to have superior bloodlines to Nellens considering that it has far more Exalted. Enough to staff the Imperial Navy, which is hardly small.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T00:41:02-07:00","id":1204462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202994#post1202994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mnemon being the architect house is new this edition I think. The house didn't really have an economic gimick as much as I can remember in previous editions.</div> </div> </div> </div> Previously on Exalted, House Mnemon was mainly known for producing Martial Artists and <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sorcerers</span></span></span>, for no apparent reason, but although it wasn't a <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">central theme, temple building and manse repair was a mentioned sideline of the house economics.</span></span></span> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThe refocus means that House Mnemon is <i>now </i>mainly known for <i>piety and craftsmanship</i>, with design and construction of temples being a foundation for their house economy.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T08:09:33-07:00","id":1204551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1202315#post1202315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the part that is unclear to me is why would the Immaculates \u2013 who are noted to harbor serious misgivings about House Cynis in general \u2013 trust <i>any</i> of the information they\u2019re given this way. It\u2019s not like it could be corroborated with audio recordings or video evidence. Ah well.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWith the preview of the Realm chapter on the Immaculate Order, I feel as though this element of House Cynis has been validated a bit, either in terms of a given monk being fairly well-practiced at telling whether or not somebody is telling them the truth, any information provided by a Cynis corresponding with or filling in the blanks of their own observations, or giving them something to specifically scrutinise by another.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would still imagine that many Immaculates have a decent ideas of what the motives of any given Cynis are, but wouldn't let that get in the way of enforcing orthopraxy if somebody is accused of something particularly heinous. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T15:51:19-07:00","id":1205402,"title":"","content":"Lore and character creation rules are all fine and dandy, but <i>let's talk about Charms for now</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> One of the things I really appreciate (which is new, I think) is that excellencies that enhance static values <i>round up</i> for the Dragon-Blooded. This means that character building choices that would've been punished harshly by a round-down system are... actually viable now! Being a <i>profoundly mediocre</i> combatant (with 2 dots and a specialization) or somebody who just wants to grab Charms with Ability 3 as a prerequisite, but not spend a specialization can still get you a perfectly serviceable Defense (Dex 4 is dirt cheap even for someone with Physical as tertiary, if you're willing to forgo Stamina 3 - which, I'm guessing, is considerably less of an opportunity cost for Dragon-Blooded characters who probably can't get 3 health levels per Ox-Body purchase at all). Likewise, choosing to play a character who is very skilled, but still has room to grow (4 dots and a specialization) or is a master of her craft but hasn't refined her skills to their utmost (5 dots, no specialization) doesn't feel like sacrificing vital capabilities (this isn't just about the extra point of Defense - the ability to raise anima off-turn without using specialized defensive Charms that may be wasted in many situations is <i>really useful</i>) on the altar of staying true to one's character concept. As somebody who enjoys playing characters who are less-than-perfect even in the areas they're supposed to be divinely gifted at, this makes me very happy.<br /> <br /> <br /> The elemental aura is an interesting mechanical gimmick which allows players to fine-tune the exact amount of complexity they want to handle in-game... or accidentally shoot themselves in the foot by picking a bunch of effects that they think are really cool but also mutually incompatible or which become impossible for them to access at bonfire. I'm still not sure how I feel about it - on one hand, it's an undeniably cool mechanic that opens up a lot of tactical and character-building depth while serving as a great balancing tool to throttle effects that would be overpowered in conjunction. On the other hand, it places a lot of responsibility in the hands of the player to accurately gauge how much micro-management they're willing to tolerate in play right at character generation, where they have no way of knowing how their choices will work out in practice. (And, of course, the players who are most likely to get frustrated by accidentally locking themselves out of a significant part of their Charm suite are <i>also </i>the ones who are the least likely to plan their Charm selection in advance to prevent that from happening). However, since the Aura is a function of native Charms only, newbies and casual players can just be advised to rely on Martial Arts and Evocations and a small handful of synergistic effects, so there is definitely an out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Signature Charms are an interesting idea that, I think, don't quite work out as well as intended. The idea is that characters can access a significant power spike in multiple abilities at a very low buy-in (most, if not all, Signature Charms have no Charm prerequisites), which should push them towards diversifying... but at the same time, most, if not all, Signature Charms have an ability prerequisite of 5, which means that any given character will probably only have a handful of them in their main areas of focus, and practically none ever in non-Aspect, non-Favored Abilities. This is really selling the potential of the concept short: I like the idea that after a certain level of enlightenment, the raw elemental Essence of these demigods pours out, unconstrained by their training, as it is fueled by a transcendent, instinctive understanding of the workings of Creation instead of human skill. But, I suppose, if I were so inclined, it would be easy enough to write up a second set of five Charms for each ability, with the minimums of Essence 4 and Ability 3, which are strong entry-level effects instead of the more specialized peaks of power represented by current sigs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":3443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","user":"aluminiumtrioxid","date":". 04-10-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T20:24:54-07:00","id":1205451,"title":"","content":"Isn't Become the Hammer hella good? This is the new dragonblooded level? What am I missing here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T21:15:06-07:00","id":1205456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1205451#post1205451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Become the Hammer hella good? This is the new dragonblooded level? What am I missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean... it is great, but it\u2019s still subject to Dragon Blooded\u2019s lower dice cap, and the excellency feature is still something you\u2019re having to buy that Solars get for free; so it\u2019s not like it\u2019s unbalanced or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T22:32:24-07:00","id":1205465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1205451#post1205451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Become the Hammer hella good? This is the new dragonblooded level? What am I missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is comparable to combining Fist of Iron Technique and Excellent Solar Brawl; for one less mote, you get to reroll-sixes-until-banished on all damage rolls rather than ignore essence+intimacy soak on withering damage rolls.<br /> <br /> \u200bCompared to Ex2's Become the Hammer, though, <i>hello yes</i>, this is the new dragonblooded level!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T23:02:59-07:00","id":1205471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1205456#post1205456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean... it is great, but it\u2019s still subject to Dragon Blooded\u2019s lower dice cap, and the excellency feature is still something you\u2019re having to buy that Solars get for free; so it\u2019s not like it\u2019s unbalanced or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, those dice caps don't mean as much when the combatants are on a budget of 5m/turn.<br /> <br /> My last fight as a Solar almost ended badly against <i>a hobgoblin and his two dogs</i>, because I didn't wanna blow through all my Essence in case I was gonna need to use it later against Hob's raksha master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-11-2018, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:37:39-07:00","id":1205503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1205451#post1205451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Become the Hammer hella good? This is the new dragonblooded level? What am I missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is what I thought when I saw it.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=c_O0jNYOGTQ\" data-code=\"c_O0jNYOGTQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/c_O0jNYOGTQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T02:00:03-07:00","id":1205508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1205451#post1205451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Become the Hammer hella good? This is the new dragonblooded level? What am I missing here?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Become the Hammer is amazing, and the nicest thing about it is that it makes Charms that grant doubles on decisive damage even better <i>for free</i>. I think it's consistent with Brawl's shtick as the killiest ability, but shouldn't necessarily be taken as representative of Dragon-Blooded power level (kinda like Increasing Strength Exercise's scenelong decisive damage boost, while in many ways a cornerstone of Solar power, isn't actually something that becomes a running theme across their entire set).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:17:42-07:00","id":1205562,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m planning to do these by splitting every ability tree in two: in part 1, we\u2019re going to talk about the Charms that are available straight out of chargen, whereas in part 2, we\u2019re going to discuss the rest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Archery</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Unobstructed Hunter\u2019s Aim:</b> at first, I did not like this Charm. I thought the excellency had a cut-rate version of Sight Without Eyes tacked on, which felt\u2026 inappropriate.<br /> <br /> Sight Without Eyes, to me, is one of those Charms that make an incredibly strong thematic statement about who Solars are and how their power manifests: it\u2019s a 1 mote Charm with a duration of One tick that eliminates any and all visual penalties on the attack roll. Contrast that with their other penalty negator, which costs 3m, has a duration of Instant, and adds some extra effects (which are undeniably powerful) \u2013 it is E2 Archery 5, as opposed to SWE\u2019s E1 Archery 3. To conquer other adverse conditions does not come as naturally to Solars as negating visual penalties does: SWE reflects the nature of Solar Essence as something that illuminates and cuts through obfuscation with contemptuous ease (used in conjunction with Trance of Unhesitating Speed, it might add up to 15 extra dice split across five attacks for a single mote!). Giving a weaker version of this to Dragon-Blooded as a built-in part of their excellency felt like the writer was <i>missing the point,</i> drawing the conclusion that SWE merely reflected the genre convention that archers are keen-eyed folks, and therefore it should be a natural, basic effect that flows from the logic of the Archery ability instead of something that reflects on the unique nature of Solars themselves.<br /> <br /> However, in the end, I find that I\u2019m okay with the rider. It\u2019s very specific (only eliminating a point of penalty when shooting at living or undead targets) and reflects the more abstract and esoteric side of the element of wood, its interpretation as life force. It also helps that this is the only Charm in Archery for negating visual penalties \u2013 if somebody wants to see through darkness and obstruction, they need to invest in Awareness, which is actually where ability logic should point us towards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sky-Calming Draw:</b> what a strange Charm. Used with the ability\u2019s namesake weapon, it doesn\u2019t actually <i>do</i> all that much: spend 4 motes and a turn aiming to negate penalties from wind and weather \u2013 this is slightly worse value than the excellency, given that even the most horrible weather conditions tend to max out at a -3 penalty, which means you\u2019re adding 3d for 4m. A fairly situational effect for those times when every die counts. However, where this Charm really shines is allowing firewand users to shoot out to Medium range. On a withering attack, it compares favorably to Righteous Devil Style\u2019s Blossom of Inevitable Demise: you get to extend your range out to Medium for 3m, and then ignore all weather penalties for a surcharge of 1m. I would not have expected an Air Aspected Charm to be all-around better with a firewand than it is with a bow, but here we are.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Death From Nowhere:</b> unless you\u2019re playing a secondary school game, this is going to be 3m for +2 damage straight out of chargen, which is\u2026 not amazing (but also not quite as terrible as 3m for a situational +1 damage, which you get with it at Essence 1). However, assuming you started out with a decent Perception, it will steadily raise in value as you gain Essence, eventually ending up with 3m for +4-5 damage, which is pretty good value, even taking its limitations into account. Another useful feature is that it\u2019s Air/Water aspected, serving as a cheap way to set up an appropriate Aura state for powerful high-Essence tricks like Horizon-Spanning Arc and Arrow Rain Tempest.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Harvest of the Hunter:</b> honestly, I\u2019ve never seen anyone use ammunition checks, so this Charm is pretty much useless to me. Luckily, none of the powerful capstone effects have this as a prerequisite, albeit a lot of pretty good early Charms do. Such as\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arrow Thorn Technique:</b> only at higher Essence does this Charm get really powerful, but when it does, the effects are spectacular. +4-5 dice of pretty much guaranteed decisive damage on an ambush? Dealing 8-10 minimum damage on a withering attack, no matter how much of a soak monster you\u2019re facing? <i>For a measly 3 motes?</i> Yes please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Boughs of Burning Autumn:</b> this compares favorably to Cloud of Ebon Devils, allowing a reflexive reload with no restrictions on the next action and no risk of failure for a 1i surcharge. It also adds some flexibility, allowing for the reloading of any Slow weapon, not just firewands, and an opportunity to build either Fire (setting up Blazing Phoenix Pinion or a powerful Dodge suite) or Wood (for the majority of high-Essence Archery tricks) Aura.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Life-Swelling Sap Strike:</b> spend 3m 1WP to force a -1 Evasion penalty on your opponent and continuously sap his Initiative at a 1/round rate (on average, equivalent to snake venom) until he or one of his allies is willing to spend an action and 4 initiative on a Gambit to cut it off. Good enough, but even better if you have a brawler buddy nearby, who can unleash a reflexive decisive to take advantage of the Evasion penalty and the extra initiative granted by the Distract. May apply to regular decisives in Wood Aura. The ability to insta-kill undead is probably never going to come up, though (this is a decisive-only effect, so the only way for this to Crash an opponent is via the torturously slow 1/round initiative sap, which takes 3 rounds to put someone into the dirt even from base \u2013 better hope they don\u2019t manage to land a successful withering in that time [j/k they totally will lol]). (I have no idea why incredibly fiddly and situational overengineered extra effects are so popular on Dragon-Blooded Charms \u2013 the fan version was full of them, too.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arbor Sentinel Technique:</b> 4m 1WP for a scenelong +2 non-Charm Defense bonus wherever there is ground? And you can\u2019t run out of arrows? This is really good. The fact that you\u2019re effectively rooted in place, less so \u2013 but guess what, the charmset has solutions that help you mitigate this problem (Unmoving Center Enlightenment jumps to mind \u2013 or you could just be an Earth Aspect, flare your anima, and knock enemies away from you without having to do anything, albeit you\u2019ll need ways to reduce your anima if you want to use high-level capstone effects). (Not to mention that you can hand over your movement actions to a buddy who has Become the Wave without feeling the slightest bit of remorse.) The only way for this Charm to be even better would be having a way to generate difficult terrain, but a custom Archery Charm or Evocations can easily cover that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Drawing Lightning Style:</b> 4m for +3 decisive damage is a very good deal \u2013 it\u2019s better than White Reaper\u2019s damage adder, for comparison -, but where this Charm really shines is combining the repurchase with Arrow Thorn Technique, potentially conjuring up 6+ dice of damage for 7 motes. That\u2019s a painful hit even from base initiative, and best of all, even though you expel your Aura in the process of making the attack, it springs right back up at the end of your turn (since you\u2019re only using a mix of Balanced and Air aspected Charms to enhance your shot).<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spring Follows Winter:</b> this is a really powerful effect. For 5m 2i, you get to increase your chances of hitting a given Defense by 10-25%, which is roughly the equivalent of +3-4 non-Charm dice (depending on the exact Difficulty). Of course, the downside is that you have to pay twice for everything that enhances your attack, so this is less about making your ultimate doomcombo unavoidable, and more about making sure that a shot for which you\u2019ve built up Initiative throughout the entire combat will actually land. (Albeit I guess it can help you make the most out of Arrow Thorn Technique, but paying a 3m surcharge for roughly +0.6 level of damage is not necessarily going to be worth it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:10:44-07:00","id":1217111,"title":"","content":"So, any progress on this one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:35:48-07:00","id":1217124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200645-oh-look-a-bandwagon-watch-me-jump-on-it-or-where-i-read-dragon-blooded-wfhw?p=1217111#post1217111